{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdeFpdti3e8SSPZotSKj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SqumSfrQwpGuBx1naYXDnA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i '' 's/cut -c1-200/cut -c1-48/' h.sh && . ./h.sh\n# B02\nc B02.1 no infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 'table/clinic-agent-*' \"\" \"The runtime role's DynamoDB statement (Get/BatchGet/Put/Update/Query) covers every table named clinic-agent-*. That includes clinic-agent-control (kill switch, main.tf:122) and clinic-agent-approvals (main.tf:97), which the agent should not be able to write. Secrets are granted as clinic-agent/* (iam.tf:35), all clinics at once.\"\nc B02.2 no src/tools/executor.ts:63 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' \"\" \"clinicId is an argument the model fills in. It picks the EHR OAuth client, the payments key and the SMS number for the call (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12, sms.ts:23). The runtime role can read every clinic's secret, so tenant scope is not in the credential. The web chat tenant also comes from an x-clinic-id header (webchat.ts:43).\"\nc B02.3 no src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:41 'body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),' \"\" \"EHR tokens are requested with scope only, no audience or resource. The eligibility exchange does set audience (eligibility-a2a.ts:43) and chat JWTs are checked for audience (webchat.ts:30). Receiving services are outside this repo.\"\nc B02.4 yes src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:41 \"subject_token: workloadToken,\" \"Searched src/ for the incoming Authorization header being forwarded: webchat.ts:23-33 only verifies it; no tool or API client reads it. Credentials come from Secrets Manager under the IRSA role or the projected workload token.\" \"Clients use the agent's own workload token and per-clinic service secrets, not a user's token.\"\nit B02 gap high \"Credentials are not scoped to one tenant: the model picks the clinic, and the runtime role reads all clinics' secrets and every clinic-agent-* table.\" \"Derive clinicId from the verified run context, ignore model and header values, and narrow the IAM resources to named tables and per-tenant secrets.\" \"Limit credentials to named operations and resources, including tenant boundaries\" \"A04,R11\"\n# B03\nc B03.1 yes src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:36 \"new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId:\" \"Searched src/ and k8s/ for AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, static keys in env and fallback to a key when Secrets Manager fails; none. ConfigMap holds only a secret ARN (deployment.yaml:42).\" \"Per-clinic client secrets are fetched at run time from Secrets Manager; pods use IRSA and a projected token.\"\nc B03.2 unknown infra/terraform/main.tf:166 'resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {' \"\" \"Token lifetimes are bounded in the repo (workload token 900 s at deployment.yaml:111, EHR access tokens 5 min, IRSA sessions 3600 s at iam.tf:5). The static vendor secrets (EHR client secret, payments key, SMS token, SMS signing secret) are created in main.tf:161-178 with no rotation resource anywhere in the repo. Rotation may be set outside Terraform.\"\nc B03.3 yes Dockerfile:12 \"ENV NODE_ENV=production\" \"Grepped the whole tree for AKIA, sk- keys, password/api_key assignments, .env files and ARG secrets; none. Prompts contain no secret values; Dockerfile ENV holds no secret.\" \"No long-lived secret literal in prompts, Dockerfile, k8s or config.\"\nc B03.4 unknown src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:18 \"checkServerIdentity: (_host: string, cert: PeerCertificate) => {\" \"\" \"README says mTLS, but the code only pins the server certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:16-25) and sends bearer tokens. No client certificate, DPoP or cert-bound token is configured. Whether the EHR, payments and SMS providers support holder binding is not stated here.\"\nit B03 needs_evidence medium \"Secrets are fetched at run time and none are checked in, but rotation and holder binding for vendor secrets are not shown in this repo.\" \"Show rotation settings for the EHR, payments, SMS and signing secrets, and whether the vendors support mTLS or DPoP binding.\"\n# B04\nc B04.1 unknown infra/terraform/iam.tf:3 'resource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {' \"\" \"The agent has its own IRSA role, which can be detached or disabled without touching a user. No revoke script or runbook is in the repo.\"\nc B04.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"Revocation of the IRSA role or EHR OAuth clients would sit in AWS IAM and the EHR, outside the agent. The repo has no deny list or gateway. The only in-repo stop path (kill-switch.ts) runs inside the agent process; that belongs to R11.\"\nc B04.3 unknown src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:34 \"if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;\" \"\" \"EHR tokens are cached up to about 5 min and MCP sessions live 4 min (ehr-mcp.ts:66-69). IRSA sessions last up to 3600 s (iam.tf:5). No maximum revocation time is stated in the repo, and how services validate tokens is outside it.\"\nc B04.4 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No revoke code or runbook in the repo, so what it covers (access tokens, sessions) cannot be read here.\"\nit B04 needs_evidence medium \"The agent has its own identity, but the revoke path, its time limit and its coverage of cached tokens are not in this repo.\" \"Document and drill revoking the clinic-agent-runtime role and EHR clients, with a stated maximum cutoff time.\"","description":"Record B02-B04 answers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1373,"cache_read_input_tokens":241248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1373},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool