plate variables come from the model, sms.ts:19). No plan-then-execute or capability tracking is in the code.\"\nfl B05 src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 \"A peer reply (depositWaived) triggers payments.refundDeposit with no approval, though payments__refund_deposit is a high-impact tool.\"\nit B05 gap high \"Cancel through ehr__update_appointment and the eligibility-triggered deposit refund both skip the approval gate.\" \"Gate all consequential actions by operation and arguments, including status=cancelled updates and refunds made inside other tools.\" \"Block them by default in the execution path\" \"\"\n# B06\nc B06.1 yes src/tools/approvals.ts:17 \"argsHash: string;\" \"Searched for a boolean-only approval; the record holds id, tool, tenantId, agentInstanceId, runId, argsHash, approvedBy, approverRole and expiresAt.\" \"The record stores instance, tool, tenant, run, args hash, approver, role and expiry.\"\nc B06.2 no src/tools/approvals.ts:75 'if (rec.tool !== req.tool) return { ok: false, reason: \"approval is for a different tool\" };' \"\" \"checkApproval compares status, tool, tenant and expiry only. argsHash, agentInstanceId and runId are stored but never compared; req.args is unused. Changed arguments or another instance pass.\"\nc B06.3 no src/tools/approvals.ts:81 \"return { ok: true, approval: rec };\" \"\" \"Approval use is never recorded: no conditional update, no consumed flag. The same approvalId can run again for 15 minutes, in parallel or later.\"\nc B06.4 no src/tools/approvals.ts:78 \"if (!rec.approverRole || !policy.approval.approverRoles.includes(rec.approverRole)) {\" \"\" \"Approver role is checked against policy.yaml. Permissions and the resource's state are not rechecked when the action runs (executor.ts:80-86 goes straight to invoke).\"\nc B06.5 yes src/tools/approvals.ts:71 \"approval store unavailable:\" \"Read the catch at approvals.ts:70-72 and its caller executor.ts:81, which denies when check.ok is false; requestApproval errors propagate and stop the call.\" \"A read error returns ok:false and the call is denied.\"\nfl B06 prompts/system.md:19 \"The approval id reaches the tool only through the model (runs keep no state), and the approval is not bound to the patient or subject who asked.\"\nit B06 gap high \"Approvals are not compared to the call's arguments or instance and are never consumed, so one approval can be replayed with different arguments.\" \"Compare argsHash, agentInstanceId and subject at execution, and mark the approval used with a conditional write.\" \"Make approvals single-use\" \"\"\n# B07\nc B07.1 yes config/budgets.yaml:3 \"maxTurns: 8\" \"Searched for unlimited values and while(true) loops; loop.ts:55 is for(;;) but budget.turn() at line 56 caps it. All six limits have numbers (turns, wall, tokens, cost, tool rate, peer calls); budgets.yaml:10 states the agent starts no sub-agents.\" \"Loop, wall time, token, cost, tool-rate and peer-call limits are set.\"\nc B07.2 yes src/agent/budget.ts:102 \"if (used > max) {\" \"Read budget.ts check/shared, loop.ts catch (95-111) and executor.ts:92: BudgetExceeded aborts the signal and stops the run; the limits come from config/budgets.yaml, not the model.\" \"The harness throws and aborts when a limit is passed; the run stops and hands off to staff.\"\nc B07.3 yes config/budgets.yaml:10 \"maxPeerCalls: 2\" \"Searched src/ for spawn, handoff, Task and create_agent; none. The only delegation is the eligibility peer, capped by budget.ts:154-157.\" \"No sub-agents exist; peer calls are counted against the run budget.\"\nc B07.4 unknown src/agent/budget.ts:139 \"await this.shared(\" \"\" \"Per-subject, per-tenant and fleet quotas are kept in DynamoDB (budget.ts:32-56, 138-162). But the intent classifier call (loop.ts:41) and count_tokens calls are not counted in cost or quotas, and run starts are not rate limited, so many short runs routed to staff use no counted budget. Provider-side spend limits are outside the repo.\"\nit B07 needs_evidence medium \"Per-run and shared quotas are enforced in code, but classifier calls and run starts are outside the counted budget.\" \"Count classifier spend in RunBudget or add a per-subject run-rate limit, then drill each limit.\"\n# B08\nc B08.1 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:168 \"podSelector: {}\" \"Read the whole NetworkPolicy: policyTypes Egress and Ingress with podSelector {} selects every pod; egress allows only kube-dns, the platform egress proxy on 3128 and 10.60.12.0/28:443; ingress only from the ingress namespace on 8080. No other policy in the repo widens it.\" \"Default-deny egress and ingress with named allowed peers.\"\nc B08.2 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:63 \"hostNetwork: false\" \"Searched manifests for 0.0.0.0/0, hostPath, docker.sock, hostPID: none. Node metadata uses IMDSv2 with hop limit 1 (main.tf:68-69). The routes are the proxy and the EHR /28; what the proxy allows is outside this repo (see B09).\" \"No broad egress, host mounts or host namespaces.\"\nc B08.3 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:169 'policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]' \"Searched src/ for URL or host checks that would stand in for isolation; none are relied on. Isolation is NetworkPolicy plus IRSA.\" \"Isolation is in NetworkPolicy and IAM, not prompt or harness code.\"\nit B08 likely_pass medium \"Namespace-wide default-deny NetworkPolicy limits egress to DNS, the egress proxy and the EHR private link.\" \"Keep the proxy allowlist under review (B09).\"","description":"Record B05-B08 answers"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01PXSjupwWxBk6YVNLN4RuCw":{"cwd":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7"}}}
