{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdeSuDn5VeNqzENK2XfQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cxPMjgWKe4TRyYCX7Qj7W","name":"Bash","input":{"command":". ./h.sh\n# R07\nc R07.1 yes src/tools/executor.ts:48 \"context: d.contextSize,\" \"Checked every audit write in src/: tool events (executor.ts base), model.decision (loop.ts:69), peer.call and payment.refund (eligibility-check.ts:34,51) and reminder.sent (reminders.ts:43) carry context. intent.classified and run.* events are not tool or model actions and carry none.\" \"Each tool action record carries the context size of its deciding model call.\"\nc R07.2 yes src/agent/context-size.ts:38 'tokens: null, status: \"unavailable\"' \"Read context-size.ts:29-47: failures give tokens null with status unavailable, never 0; the reminder job also records null/unavailable (reminders.ts:43). cachedInputTokens uses ?? 0 at line 44 when the provider omits the cache field; the total itself is always from reported usage.\" \"Values are labelled measured, estimated or unavailable; missing is null.\"\nc R07.3 yes src/agent/context-size.ts:45 \"const total = usage.input_tokens + cacheRead\" \"Read the stated method (context-size.ts:3-17, 26-27): sum of uncached, cache-read and cache-creation input of one call, with cached share kept separate and compacted always false because the harness never compacts (checked loop.ts: messages are only appended).\" \"The count is a stated per-call method that includes cache and records compaction.\"\nc R07.4 yes src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:34 \"context: opts.context,\" \"Followed the value through executeTool (executor.ts:86 passes context to tool.invoke), the eligibility workflow (lines 34 and 51) and the audit schema (recorder.ts:41-49); each record also carries the traceparent and tool id.\" \"Context size is handed to tools and stored with identity and trace fields.\"\nit R07 likely_pass medium \"Every tool and model decision record carries a labelled, null-safe context size from a stated counting method.\" \"Capture short, long and cached contexts at runtime (recipe R07).\"\n# R08\nfor n in 1 2 3; do c R08.$n unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No security detection rules or alert routing are in this repo; only metrics.increment in server.ts:12-16 for identity mismatch and SMS signature failure. Rules would live in the platform SIEM.\"; done\nit R08 needs_evidence medium \"Denials are logged, but security rules and responder routing are not in this repo.\" \"Show rules for encoded payloads, outbound traffic, out-of-scope writes, escalation and repeated denials with a named responder.\"\n# R09\nc R09.1 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No detection rules in this repo.\"\nc R09.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No detection rules in this repo; only budget limits (config/budgets.yaml) cap fan-out.\"\nc R09.3 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No detection rules or per-context thresholds in this repo.\"\nc R09.4 no src/agent/loop.ts:90 \"for (const call of toolUses) {\" \"\" \"A hijacked run can do harm with allowed, ungated tools (book, update, send), and no checker compares a high-impact action with the original task before it runs.\"\nit R09 gap medium \"No pre-action check compares high-impact actions with the original task, though allowed tools alone can cause harm.\" \"Add a task-alignment check that does not see tool output, and sequence rules per context-size range.\" \"check each high-impact action against the original task before it runs\"\nit R10 needs_evidence low \"Code cannot show misalignment review; whether deliberate misalignment is in scope is not recorded.\" \"Record whether misalignment is in scope; if so, test a reviewer on evasive traces.\"\n# R11\nc R11.1 yes src/agent/loop.ts:57 \"await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\" \"Checked the loop (loop.ts:39,57), every tool call (executor.ts:59) and the reminder job (reminders.ts:29,33). A table read error throws Halted (kill-switch.ts:52-54). BatchGet UnprocessedKeys is not inspected (kill-switch.ts:24-38), a small fail-open edge.\" \"Model turns and tool calls check the stop flag; read errors halt.\"\nc R11.2 no infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 'table/clinic-agent-*' \"\" \"The runtime role may PutItem and UpdateItem on every clinic-agent-* table, and clinic-agent-control (main.tf:122) matches. The agent's own credentials can set or clear halted, though kill-switch.ts:5-7 says it only reads.\"\nc R11.3 yes src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 \"a.abort.abort(new Halted(\" \"Checked that the aborted controller is the budget signal passed to model calls (loop.ts:61) and tool.invoke (executor.ts:86), to EHR callTool (ehr-mcp.ts:95) and to payments, SMS and eligibility fetches.\" \"The watcher aborts in-flight calls through the shared abort signal within a 2 s poll.\"\nc R11.4 unknown src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:65 \"sessions.set(clinicId, client);\" \"\" \"EHR MCP sessions are cached for up to 4 minutes and not closed when a run is halted; whether they hold open streams is not visible here.\"\nc R11.5 no infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 'table/clinic-agent-*' \"\" \"A named operator role exists (iam.tf:60-86, SSO on-call group), but the agent's runtime role can also write the control table, so not only named operators can set the stop.\"\nit R11 gap high \"The agent's own runtime role can write the kill-switch table.\" \"Scope the runtime role to named tables with read-only access to clinic-agent-control.\" \"The agent's credentials must not be able to change it.\" \"B02\"\n# R12\nc R12.1 no \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No code or config states, per operation (booking, cancel, refund, SMS), whether it can be cancelled, completed or only reconciled after a stop.\"\nc R12.2 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:125 \"backoffLimit: 0\" \"Searched src/ for queues, retry loops and backoff; the only retry is the SDK's maxRetries 1 on model calls (loop.ts:15). The reminder job stops on Halted (reminders.ts:48-51).\" \"No queue exists; the cron job has no retries and halts on stop.\"\nc R12.3 no src/integrations/payments.ts:39 \"if (!res.ok) throw new Error(\" \"\" \"A timeout or abort on a refund or SMS send is recorded as tool.failed (executor.ts:93) with no marker that the outcome is unknown, no tracked hold, and no block on dependent actions.\"\nc R12.4 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:133 \"restartPolicy: Never\" \"Runs keep no checkpoint or queue (README.md:26) and the cron job never restarts (line 133, backoffLimit 0); pods restarting only start a fresh server.\" \"A stopped run is not resumed; new runs check the stop flag.\"\nc R12.5 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No workers or queued jobs hold their own tokens; pods keep IRSA credentials until the platform revokes the role.\"\nit R12 gap medium \"No per-operation stop policy or tracked hold exists for outside effects that may have happened when the stop arrived.\" \"Record per operation whether it is cancelled, completed or reconciled, and mark unknown outcomes for operator review.\" \"Where you can't cancel something, show how you check and fix the result (reconcile)\"\n# R13\nc R13.1 no src/tools/executor.ts:89 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' \"\" \"The executed record has tool, ids and approval, but no key arguments and no result summary (detail holds only clinicId). It is also written after the tool has run.\"\nc R13.2 no src/tools/executor.ts:47 \"policyVersion: policy.version,\" \"\" \"config.ts:8 types Policy.version, but config/policy.yaml:2 names the key policyVersion, so policy.version is undefined and the audit schema (recorder.ts:38) accepts the missing value. No audit record carries the policy version, on allows or denials.\"\nc R13.3 yes src/tools/executor.ts:89 'event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId' \"Checked the executed path (line 82 sets approvalId from the checked approval) and the approval request path (line 77); no other approved-run record exists.\" \"Executed records carry the approval id.\"\nc R13.4 no src/tools/executor.ts:93 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.failed\", approvalId, reason: (err as Error).message.slice(0, 300) });' \"\" \"Failures are recorded, but SDK retries are not, a timeout is logged like any failure with no unknown-outcome marker, and the tool-use id is the only operation id sent (refunds add an idempotency key, SMS and EHR writes do not).\"\nc R13.5 yes src/tools/executor.ts:51 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.denied\", reason });' \"Checked the allowlist (no audit tool exists) and the run flow: records are written by loop.ts and executor.ts, and run.stopped is written in the catch (loop.ts:107), not from the final answer.\" \"The harness writes audit records, including on denial and failure.\"\nfl R13 src/tools/executor.ts:86 \"The tool runs (line 86) before the tool.executed audit (line 89); if the audit write fails, AuditUnavailable is rethrown (line 92) after a side effect already happened, so the action is unrecorded.\"\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H006 --verdict=dismissed --reason=\"Run-start audit (loop.ts:36) precedes the try; audit failures in the try throw AuditUnavailable to the catch and stop the run before any tool runs, and error and stop paths also write records (loop.ts:107).\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H007 --verdict=dismissed --reason=\"Same block as H006: intent.classified is audited before routing and a failure stops the run; nothing proceeds on an audit error.\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H008 --verdict=dismissed --reason=\"This writes run.stopped while the run is already stopping; a failure is logged with the reason and no action proceeds.\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H009 --verdict=confirmed --item=R13 --reason=\"executeTool runs tool.invoke (line 86) before the tool.executed audit (line 89), so an audit outage after the side effect leaves it unrecorded.\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\n$PY $S/answer.py $F 