{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdeWWknGggiBfVntDcJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JxhQoMj6NTj1TDihkf2n7n","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7 && . ./h.sh\nc R12.1 no src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 \"a.abort.abort(new Halted(\" \"\" \"No code or config states, per operation (booking, cancel, refund, SMS), whether it can be cancelled, completed or only reconciled after a stop; the stop path only aborts in-flight calls.\"\n# A01\nc A01.1 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:60 \"serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\" \"Searched the repo for other uses of this service account and role: only the agent pods and its own reminder CronJob (line 131, same role at line 27) use them; there is no default or shared backend identity.\" \"Dedicated service account bound to the clinic-agent-runtime IAM role.\"\nc A01.2 yes src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:41 \"subject_token: workloadToken,\" \"Searched src/ for the request Authorization header being forwarded; webchat.ts:23-33 only verifies it. EHR, payments and SMS use per-clinic secrets from Secrets Manager (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12, sms.ts:23).\" \"Clients use the agent's own workload token or service secrets.\"\nc A01.3 yes src/tools/executor.ts:44 \"subject: ctx.subject,\" \"Read identity.ts:56-59 and the audit writer: the user is carried as subject (patient, staff or system) next to the agent's own identity fields. The eligibility exchange keeps the workload token as subject_token and puts clinic and patient in scope (eligibility-a2a.ts:39-45).\" \"The user is carried as a separate subject on every action; the agent stays the actor.\"\nc A01.4 yes infra/terraform/iam.tf:25 'resource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {' \"Read iam.tf:3-57: the policy is attached to role clinic-agent-runtime, assumable only by the two agent service accounts (lines 14-17); no user or group grant is involved.\" \"Permissions are bound to the agent role, which can be removed alone.\"\nit A01 likely_pass medium \"The agent has its own service account and IAM role, and users are carried only as a subject.\" \"Run the A01 revocation drill.\"\n# A02\nc A02.1 yes src/audit/recorder.ts:8 \"export const IdentityFields = z.object({\" \"Read the schema (recorder.ts:8-15): accountableParty, operationalOwner, tenantId, agentTypeId, agentInstanceId and traceparent are all required and validated before any send (line 60).\" \"All six fields are required by the audit schema.\"\nc A02.2 no src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:57 'if (!parsed.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \"invalid payload\" });' \"\" \"Refusals before a run starts write no record: invalid SMS payload (line 57), unknown number (61), and the web chat 401, 400 and 404 returns (webchat.ts:24,36,40,45). Run, tool, denied, failed and reminder paths do carry all six fields.\"\nc A02.3 yes src/audit/recorder.ts:14 \"traceparent: z.string().regex(\" \"Checked that every writer spreads ctx.identity() (loop.ts:33, executor.ts:42, reminders.ts:37), which sets traceparent (identity.ts:110).\" \"traceparent is a field of the audit record itself.\"\nc A02.4 no src/routes/webchat.ts:43 'const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;' \"\" \"The audit tenantId comes from RunContext, which the web chat builds from a caller-supplied x-clinic-id header ahead of the verified token claim.\"\nit A02 gap medium \"Audit tenant can come from an unprotected header, and refusals before a run are not recorded.\" \"Take the tenant from the verified token only, and audit pre-run refusals with the six fields.\" \"every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context\" \"A04\"\n# A03\nc A03.1 no src/agent/identity.ts:24 '.filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))' \"\" \"The type id hashes only prompts/*.txt, so prompts/system.md, the system prompt, is not part of it. Image digest, harness version and sha, models and three config files are included.\"\nc A03.2 no src/agent/identity.ts:24 '.filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))' \"\" \"The extension filter skips system.md; release/manifest.json and the MCP server list are not hashed either. A changed system prompt keeps the same type id.\"\nc A03.3 yes src/config.ts:49 'export const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";' \"Searched src/ and config/ for aliases, env overrides and -latest; both models are dated constants (config.ts:49-50) and the manifest marks them pinned_snapshot (release/manifest.json:21,30).\" \"Dated snapshot ids, no alias or env fallback.\"\nc A03.4 yes src/agent/identity.ts:25 \".sort();\" \"Read identity.ts:16-46: fixed part order, sorted prompt file list, labelled and NUL-delimited parts, config files in a fixed array.\" \"Parts are labelled, delimited and sorted before hashing.\"\nc A03.5 yes src/agent/identity.ts:8 'const CONFIG_FILES = [\"config/policy.yaml\", \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\", \"config/budgets.yaml\"];' \"Listed every hashed input: digest, versions, prompt files, model ids and three config files; none holds secrets, and no environment is dumped.\" \"No secret values are hashed.\"\nit A03 gap high \"The type id skips prompts/system.md because it only hashes .txt files, so the system prompt can change without changing the id.\" \"Hash every file under prompts/ (and the MCP server list), then add a test that changing each input changes the id.\" \"hash of the container digest, harness, system prompt, model ID and version, and configuration\" \"C03\"\n# A04\nc A04.1 no src/tools/executor.ts:63 'const clinicId = typeof input.clinicId === \"string\" && input.clinicId ? input.clinicId : ctx.tenantId;' \"\" \"The tenant used for tool calls and approvals is a model-supplied clinicId when present. The web chat tenant comes from a request header (webchat.ts:43).\"\nc A04.2 no src/tools/executor.ts:22 'const CONTROL_ARGS = new Set([\"approvalId\", \"clinicId\"]);' \"\" \"A tenant label in tool arguments is not rejected or overwritten: clinicId is read as an override (line 63) and then removed from the forwarded args. The code comment says this is intended for staff, but the model can set it for any run, including patient runs.\"\nc A04.3 yes src/agent/identity.ts:70 \"subject: Subject;\" \"Read the audit schema (recorder.ts:35) and writers: subject (kind and id) is stored apart from the agent identity fields on every event.\" \"A separate subject field holds the user or system.\"\nc A04.4 yes src/workers/reminders.ts:25 'subject: { kind: \"system\", id: \"reminders-cron\" }' \"Searched src/ for queue producers, SQS, jobs and enqueue calls; none. The cron job builds its own verified RunContext and writes the six fields (reminders.ts:36-45).\" \"The one background job builds its own context; no queue exists.\"\nc A04.5 no src/routes/webchat.ts:43 'const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;' \"\" \"A caller header chooses which clinic's data and secrets the run uses, ahead of the signed token claim.\"\nit A04 gap high \"The clinic for a run can be set by a request header or a model-chosen tool argument instead of verified context.\" \"Use the token's clinic_id (and the number's clinic for SMS) only, and delete the clinicId override.\" \"Don't accept labels the model supplies.\" \"B02,A02\"\n# A05\nc A05.1 unknown release/manifest.json:4 '\"agentTypeId\":' \"\" \"Audit records carry agentTypeId and agentInstanceId (recorder.ts:12-13). Only the current release file is in the repo; a store keyed by type id for older releases and a map from instance id to live pods are not shown.\"\nc A05.2 yes src/config.ts:63 'accountableParty: \"northbay-clinic-group:patient-access\",' \"Looked for an ownership file: CODEOWNERS covers paths, README.md:72-73 names the accountable party and #agent-platform-oncall, and config.ts:63-64 puts both values into every audit record; manifest.json:43,52 name owners of the EHR and peer.\" \"Accountable party and operational owner are in code and docs.\"\nc A05.3 unknown src/control/kill-switch.ts:57 'if (halted.has(\"global\")) throw new Halted(\"global\");' \"\" \"The kill switch scopes are global and one clinic. A single instance or the agent type could be contained by scaling the deployment or revoking the role, which is platform action outside this repo.\"\nit A05 needs_evidence medium \"Records carry type and instance ids and owners, but per-instance containment and the manifest lookup are not shown here.\" \"Run the A05 drill: from one trace id find the manifest, owner and pod, and contain only that pod.\"\n# A06\nfor n in 1 2 3 4; do c A06.$n unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"The agent starts no sub-agents (config/budgets.yaml:10); the eligibility agent is an independent peer called with structured data, so no parent prompt or child ids apply.\"; done\nit A06 na_candidate medium \"The agent has no sub-agents or handoffs; the eligibility peer is called with structured data.\" \"Governance to confirm the eligibility peer is not a delegated sub-agent.\"\n# A07\nc A07.1 yes release/manifest.json:27 '\"role\": \"intent_classifier\",' \"Searched src/ for model calls: classifier.ts:45 (Haiku), loop.ts:60-61 (Sonnet agent and its count_tokens). No embedding, reranker or judge call exists; the manifest lists both models.\" \"The classifier is the only helper model and is in the manifest.\"\nc A07.2 yes src/agent/classifier.ts:19 \".update(CLASSIFIER_PROMPT)\" \"Read classifier.ts:13-22: CLASSIFIER_ID hashes the pinned model id, prompt and config; the model is a dated snapshot (config.ts:50) and is part of the agent type id (identity.ts:30).\" \"The classifier id covers pinned model, prompt and config.\"\nc A07.3 yes src/agent/loop.ts:42 'await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });' \"Checked that classifyIntent returns classifierId, requestedModel and servedModel on every branch, including failures (classifier.ts:57-76).\" \"Every classifier decision, pass or fail, is audited with its id and served model.\"\nc A07.4 yes src/agent/classifier.ts:60 \"if (res.model !== CLASSIFIER_MODEL) {\" \"Read every branch (classifier.ts:55-76): timeout, API error, served-model mismatch, invalid or unknown output and low confidence all return route staff; tests cover them (controls.test.ts:109-120).\" \"Any classifier failure routes the message to staff.\"\nit A07 likely_pass medium \"The one helper model is listed, pinned, identified and audited, and any failure routes to staff.\" \"Swap and time out the classifier in a drill (recipe A07).\"","description":"Record A01-A07 answers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3065,"cache_read_input_tokens":272366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3065},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be046cb2-a615-4b99-9b5b-9574ded4eee7","uuid":"c727ea9c-2247-4a55-b4d3-007efe84fa39","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:29:09.535Z","request_id":"req_011CfdeWWHWj3WFLxxzLQed6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JxhQoMj6NTj1TDihkf2n7n":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7 && . ./h.sh\nc R12.1 no src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 \"a.abort.abort(new Halted(\" \"\" \"No code or config states, per operation (booking, cancel, refund, SMS), whether it can be cancelled, completed or only reconciled after a stop; the stop path only aborts in-flight calls.\"\n# A01\nc A01.1 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:60 \"serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\" \"Searched the repo for other uses of this service account and role: only the agent pods