one. The cron job builds its own verified RunContext and writes the six fields (reminders.ts:36-45).\" \"The one background job builds its own context; no queue exists.\"\nc A04.5 no src/routes/webchat.ts:43 'const tenantId = (req.headers[\"x-clinic-id\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;' \"\" \"A caller header chooses which clinic's data and secrets the run uses, ahead of the signed token claim.\"\nit A04 gap high \"The clinic for a run can be set by a request header or a model-chosen tool argument instead of verified context.\" \"Use the token's clinic_id (and the number's clinic for SMS) only, and delete the clinicId override.\" \"Don't accept labels the model supplies.\" \"B02,A02\"\n# A05\nc A05.1 unknown release/manifest.json:4 '\"agentTypeId\":' \"\" \"Audit records carry agentTypeId and agentInstanceId (recorder.ts:12-13). Only the current release file is in the repo; a store keyed by type id for older releases and a map from instance id to live pods are not shown.\"\nc A05.2 yes src/config.ts:63 'accountableParty: \"northbay-clinic-group:patient-access\",' \"Looked for an ownership file: CODEOWNERS covers paths, README.md:72-73 names the accountable party and #agent-platform-oncall, and config.ts:63-64 puts both values into every audit record; manifest.json:43,52 name owners of the EHR and peer.\" \"Accountable party and operational owner are in code and docs.\"\nc A05.3 unknown src/control/kill-switch.ts:57 'if (halted.has(\"global\")) throw new Halted(\"global\");' \"\" \"The kill switch scopes are global and one clinic. A single instance or the agent type could be contained by scaling the deployment or revoking the role, which is platform action outside this repo.\"\nit A05 needs_evidence medium \"Records carry type and instance ids and owners, but per-instance containment and the manifest lookup are not shown here.\" \"Run the A05 drill: from one trace id find the manifest, owner and pod, and contain only that pod.\"\n# A06\nfor n in 1 2 3 4; do c A06.$n unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"The agent starts no sub-agents (config/budgets.yaml:10); the eligibility agent is an independent peer called with structured data, so no parent prompt or child ids apply.\"; done\nit A06 na_candidate medium \"The agent has no sub-agents or handoffs; the eligibility peer is called with structured data.\" \"Governance to confirm the eligibility peer is not a delegated sub-agent.\"\n# A07\nc A07.1 yes release/manifest.json:27 '\"role\": \"intent_classifier\",' \"Searched src/ for model calls: classifier.ts:45 (Haiku), loop.ts:60-61 (Sonnet agent and its count_tokens). No embedding, reranker or judge call exists; the manifest lists both models.\" \"The classifier is the only helper model and is in the manifest.\"\nc A07.2 yes src/agent/classifier.ts:19 \".update(CLASSIFIER_PROMPT)\" \"Read classifier.ts:13-22: CLASSIFIER_ID hashes the pinned model id, prompt and config; the model is a dated snapshot (config.ts:50) and is part of the agent type id (identity.ts:30).\" \"The classifier id covers pinned model, prompt and config.\"\nc A07.3 yes src/agent/loop.ts:42 'await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \"intent.classified\", detail: { ...intent } });' \"Checked that classifyIntent returns classifierId, requestedModel and servedModel on every branch, including failures (classifier.ts:57-76).\" \"Every classifier decision, pass or fail, is audited with its id and served model.\"\nc A07.4 yes src/agent/classifier.ts:60 \"if (res.model !== CLASSIFIER_MODEL) {\" \"Read every branch (classifier.ts:55-76): timeout, API error, served-model mismatch, invalid or unknown output and low confidence all return route staff; tests cover them (controls.test.ts:109-120).\" \"Any classifier failure routes the message to staff.\"\nit A07 likely_pass medium \"The one helper model is listed, pinned, identified and audited, and any failure routes to staff.\" \"Swap and time out the classifier in a drill (recipe A07).\"","description":"Record A01-A07 answers"}}}
