{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdeZHC38gfB3Gj4btodZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016t9abdBec6NEUrTsDsneMr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7 && . ./h.sh\n# C01\nc C01.1 yes release/manifest.json:64 '\"budgets\": \"config/budgets.yaml\",' \"Compared the manifest with configuration: container, harness, prompts, models, MCP servers, native tools, scopes, memory and retrieval (none), network policy, budgets, action policy version, peers and the AWS role are all listed. No rules files exist to list.\" \"The manifest covers the listed release categories.\"\nc C01.2 yes release/manifest.json:27 '\"role\": \"intent_classifier\",' \"Searched src/ for model ids: only the agent and the classifier (config.ts:49-50); both have records with provider, requestedId, versionDoc and adapter.\" \"Both models have records with provider, id, snapshot kind and adapter.\"\nc C01.3 yes release/manifest.json:21 '\"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",' \"Read both model records (lines 18-35): each has kind pinned_snapshot and a versionDoc url with a checked date of 2026-09-15.\" \"Both ids are labelled with the provider doc and date.\"\nc C01.4 no release/manifest.json:5 '\"repository\": \"418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent\",' \"\" \"Only the EHR server and eligibility peer name an owner (manifest.json:43,52). The image, prompts, both models, native tools and harness have no named owner, though digests, hashes and a git sha are present.\"\nc C01.5 yes release/manifest.json:23 '\"adapter\": null,' \"Searched the tree for training, fine-tune and Trainer code and for datasets; none. Both models are hosted provider snapshots.\" \"No self-run training exists.\"\nit C01 gap medium \"Most manifest artifacts, including the image, prompts and models, have no named owner.\" \"Add an owner per artifact in release/manifest.json.\" \"Name each artifact's owner and a reference that can't change, where one exists.\"\n# C02\nc C02.1 yes infra/terraform/github.tf:26 \"required_approving_review_count\" \"Searched src/ for runtime fetches of prompts, policy or tool config; all load from files in the image (config.ts:44-47, loop.ts:14). Branch protection requires 2 approvals and code owner review (github.tf:26-27).\" \"Config is in git; merges need two reviews and code owners.\"\nc C02.2 yes .github/CODEOWNERS:4 \"/prompts/\" \"Read CODEOWNERS: production config paths (prompts, config, release, infra, k8s, .github) are limited to platform-leads and cloud-security; deploy uses protected environments with named reviewers (github.tf:38-62). The * dev team owns only unlisted source paths.\" \"Production config paths have named owners and a protected deploy environment.\"\nc C02.3 yes .github/workflows/deploy.yml:48 'test -n \"$OWNER\"' \"Read the emergency job (deploy.yml:41-51, 82-99): owner, reason, an end date and a hotfix/* branch are required, and a follow-up review issue is opened for the owner.\" \"Emergency deploys record owner, reason, end date and a follow-up issue.\"\nit C02 likely_pass medium \"Changes need review and code owners, and emergency deploys record owner, reason, end date and follow-up.\" \"Try an unauthorised prompt change and an emergency drill (recipe C02).\"\n# C03\nc C03.1 yes k8s/deployment.yaml:76 \"clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\" \"Followed models (dated constants, config.ts:49-50) and prompts (copied into the image, Dockerfile:17); no tag or alias fallback.\" \"Image, prompts and models are fixed by digest or dated id.\"\nc C03.2 unknown src/server.ts:32 \"if (typeId !== manifest.agentTypeId) {\" \"\" \"The only comparison runs inside the agent process at startup. CI checks prompt files against the manifest, not the running pods, and deploy.yml only greps the digest. A platform observer is not shown.\"\nc C03.3 no src/agent/identity.ts:24 '.filter((f) => f.endsWith(\".txt\"))' \"\" \"The id is computed from files at start, but prompts/system.md is skipped, so a changed system prompt still yields the approved id.\"\nc C03.4 yes release/manifest.json:23 '\"adapter\": null,' \"Searched for from_pretrained, torch.load, weights downloads and adapters; none. Models are hosted Anthropic snapshots.\" \"No self-hosted weights or adapters.\"\nc C03.5 no src/server.ts:33 'app.log.error({ expected: manifest.agentTypeId, actual: typeId }, \"agent type id does not match release manifest\");' \"\" \"A mismatch logs an error and a metric (lines 33-34), then startup continues (setAgentTypeId at line 36 and listen at line 90). Nothing blocks or quarantines.\"\nit C03 gap high \"A changed system prompt keeps the approved agent-type-id, and an identity mismatch only logs.\" \"Hash every prompt file and exit on mismatch, plus an outside check of running artifacts.\" \"Test that a changed prompt, model, weights file, or tool setup can't keep showing the old approved identity without being caught.\" \"A03\"\n# C04\nfor n in 1 2 3; do c C04.$n unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No drift detection (GitOps, config rules, scheduled comparison) is in this repo; only the startup type-id comparison in server.ts:32.\"; done\nit C04 needs_evidence medium \"No drift detector is shown in this repo.\" \"Show per-deployment drift checks for images, prompts, MCP list, permissions and egress with alert and response times.\"\n# C05\nc C05.1 unknown package.json:17 '\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",' \"\" \"Direct dependencies are pinned to exact versions (package.json:17-35), but no package-lock.json is in the tree though Dockerfile:4 and ci.yml:20 run npm ci with one. Transitive pins cannot be read.\"\nc C05.2 yes src/config.ts:49 'export const AGENT_MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\";' \"Searched src/ and config/ for model ids, env overrides and aliases; both are dated constants (config.ts:49-50) and the pricing table keys on the same ids (budgets.yaml:21-22).\" \"Both model ids are dated snapshots.\"\nc C05.3 yes release/manifest.json:23 '\"adapter\": null,' \"Searched for weights, adapter and dataset loads; none, models are hosted.\" \"No self-hosted artifacts to sign-check.\"\nc C05.4 yes release/manifest.json:32 '\"adapter\": null,' \"Grepped for pickle, torch.load, joblib and .pkl; none.\" \"No pickle-based model loads.\"\nc C05.5 yes src/agent/loop.ts:71 \"servedModel: res.model,\" \"Read loop.ts:59-76 and classifier.ts:60-76: the response model is stored as servedModel, apart from the requested id, for both models.\" \"Served model is recorded separately.\"\nit C05 needs_evidence medium \"Models are pinned, but the lockfile that pins transitive dependencies is not in the tree.\" \"Provide package-lock.json and show provider-notice and re-test process.\"\n# C06\nc C06.1 no .github/workflows/deploy.yml:35 \"deploy:\" \"\" \"ci.yml runs unit tests on source (lines 20-23) and the image job needs them (line 46), but the deploy workflow has no needs on tests and nothing runs a suite against the candidate manifest digest or model ids.\"\nc C06.2 no test/controls.test.ts:13 'describe(\"tool registry identity\", () => {' \"\" \"Tests cover budgets, the registry, the metadata scanner and the classifier. There are none for destructive-action denial, approvals, tenant limits, injection containment, audit attribution or the kill switch.\"\nc C06.3 no .github/workflows/ci.yml:22 \"- run: npm test\" \"\" \"Test results stay in CI logs; no step stores them against the manifest digest or type id.\"\nit C06 gap high \"The release suite has no attack, approval, access-limit, audit or stop tests and its results are not tied to the candidate manifest.\" \"Add those test categories and a release gate that stores results per manifest.\" \"Before promotion, run typical allowed tasks and attack cases against the release candidate.\"\n# C07\nc C07.1 no .github/workflows/deploy.yml:71 \"- name: Apply\" \"\" \"Deploys apply one manifest; no rollback script, pipeline or runbook for an earlier release is in the repo.\"\nc C07.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No rollback procedure exists to read; credentials live in Secrets Manager and IAM, outside the artifacts.\"\nc C07.3 no \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No rollback steps cover state or queued work. The agent keeps no memory or queue, but approvals and budgets live in DynamoDB and nothing says how rollback treats them.\"\nc C07.4 no release/manifest.json:22 '\"checked\": \"2026-09-15\"' \"\" \"Model records give a docs check date but no retirement date for either hosted model.\"\nit C07 gap medium \"No rollback procedure or model retirement dates are in the repo.\" \"Write and drill a rollback to the prior digest with state, credentials and retirement dates.\" \"Keep an approved recovery setup and show that rollback works.\"\n# C08\nc C08.1 unknown release/manifest.json:4 '\"agentTypeId\":' \"\" \"Audit records carry agentTypeId (recorder.ts:12). Only the current manifest is in the repo; a store keyed by type id for past releases is not shown.\"\nc C08.2 yes src/agent/loop.ts:69 \"context: contextSize,\" \"Checked every model call path: loop.ts:59-76 audits each decision with context; the classifier call has no tool action and the reminder job has no model.\" \"Each agent model decision is audited with its context size.\"\nc C08.3 yes config/budgets.yaml:10 \"this agent starts no sub-agents\" \"Searched src/ for spawn, handoff and child-agent code; none.\" \"No sub-agent prompts exist to store.\"\nc C08.4 unknown infra/terraform/main.tf:144 \"years = 7\" \"\" \"Audit objects are locked for 7 years. Retention for manifests and prompt links, and role-based read access to the audit bucket, are not set in this repo.\"\nit C08 needs_evidence medium \"Audit retention is set, but manifest lookup and access control for linked artifacts are not shown.\" \"Show manifest archive keyed by type id and access policy for audit data.\