{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfdeeR5hDTehp2VnUZNeV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XVnSWQyGC8iuLZCkdjQeJg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":". ./h.sh\nc E01.3 no src/integrations/payments.ts:9 'const BASE = process.env.PAYMENTS_API ?? \"https://api.payments-provider.example/v2\";' \"\" \"The payments API, SMS API (sms.ts:8), STS (config.ts:62), chat JWKS (config.ts:59) and the Anthropic API are called but are not in release/manifest.json or any other inventory.\"\n# E02\nc E02.1 unknown package.json:17 '\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",' \"\" \"Direct dependencies and images are pinned exactly, but no package-lock.json is in the tree. The EHR MCP server is a remote vendor service pinned by certificate (manifest.json:42), with no implementation version.\"\nc E02.2 unknown .github/workflows/ci.yml:20 \"- run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\" \"\" \"Image signing and verification exist (ci.yml:73, deploy.yml:66). No npm provenance or signature check is run for packages.\"\nc E02.3 no .github/workflows/ci.yml:22 \"- run: npm test\" \"\" \"ci.yml steps are install, lint, test, build and image; there is no npm audit, osv-scanner, trivy or grype step, and the ECR scan_on_push (main.tf:92) does not gate the build.\"\nc E02.4 no release/manifest.json:43 '\"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"' \"\" \"No approval record names publisher, permissions and update source for each dependency; the manifest has owner and certificate pin for the EHR server only.\"\nit E02 gap medium \"No vulnerability scan gates the build and no dependency approval records exist.\" \"Add an audit or osv scan that fails the build and record publisher, permissions and update source per dependency.\" \"known vulnerabilities\"\n# E03\nc E03.1 no src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 \"c.listTools(),\" \"\" \"Tools are listed from the EHR server and passed to the registry. No hash of an approved tool's description and schema is stored anywhere (searched src/ and release/).\"\nc E03.2 no src/tools/registry.ts:107 \"const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\" \"\" \"registerMcp checks only the server id, then the metadata scan. There is no fingerprint compare on load, refresh or reconnect, and no list_changed handler exists (searched src/).\"\nc E03.3 no src/tools/registry.ts:126 \"for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\" \"\" \"Any tool that passes the text scan is registered with its current definition; a changed description or schema is accepted if it is clean.\"\nc E03.4 no release/manifest.json:42 '\"tlsCertSha256\"' \"\" \"The EHR MCP server is pinned by certificate only. No implementation version or attestation is recorded apart from a metadata fingerprint, and the vendor's code cannot be seen.\"\nfl E03 src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 \"Tool list loaded from the server with no comparison to an approved fingerprint (pre-scan H011).\"\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H011 --verdict=confirmed --item=E03 --reason=\"listTools() results go straight to scanServer and into the registry; no stored fingerprint is compared.\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\nit E03 gap high \"Tool descriptions and schemas from the EHR server are scanned but never compared with an approved fingerprint.\" \"Store a hash of each approved tool's description and schema and block on mismatch at load, refresh and list-changed.\" \"Take a fingerprint of each approved tool's description and schema.\"\n# E04\nc E04.1 yes src/tools/registry.ts:114 \"scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\" \"Traced every path that loads MCP metadata: server.ts:48-49 is the only caller of registerMcp. Scanned fields: instructions, prompts, resource templates (metadata-scan.ts:100-115), tool name, title, description, input and output schemas and annotations (lines 119-126). Native tools are written in-house (executor.ts:100-183).\" \"All server metadata fields are scanned before tools reach the model.\"\nc E04.2 yes src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:41 \"const RULES: Array<{ rule: string; re: RegExp }> = [\" \"Read the rules (lines 41-58) and LIMITS (33-39): control and invisible characters, role overrides and markers, concealment, precondition injection, base64 and hex blobs, escaped unicode, URLs, emails, phone numbers, references to other servers' tools (line 67-70), and length limits.\" \"The rules cover each required category and length limits.\"\nc E04.3 yes src/tools/registry.ts:123 \"for (const [tool, findings] of scan.rejectedTools) {\" \"Read registry.ts:119-134: a server finding rejects the server, a tool finding rejects only that tool, and only acceptedTools are added.\" \"Flagged tools and servers are rejected, not just logged.\"\nc E04.4 yes src/tools/registry.ts:116 \"metadata scan error\" \"Checked registry.ts:112-118 (error rejects the server) and server.ts:47-52 (catalog failure disables EHR tools); test controls.test.ts:86-92 covers a throwing scanner. No flag turns the scan off.\" \"A scanner error rejects the whole server.\"\nit E04 likely_pass medium \"A metadata scanner covers every field, rejects flagged items, and fails closed on error.\" \"Run poisoned-metadata fixtures against the live server (recipe E04).\"\n# E05\nc E05.1 yes src/tools/registry.ts:128 'key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,' \"Checked that serverId comes from the manifest id used when the pinned connection is made (server.ts:40-49, ehr-mcp.ts:16-25); reportedName is only logged (registry.ts:109).\" \"Keys are the manifest server id plus tool name.\"\nc E05.2 yes src/tools/registry.ts:151 \"if (editDistanceAtMostOne(canonical(existing.name), c)) {\" \"Read add() (lines 137-158): duplicates and lookalikes (case, digit and rn/vv confusables, edit distance one) across servers are rejected and recorded as conflicts; tests cover them (controls.test.ts:13-45).\" \"Duplicate and lookalike names across servers are flagged and rejected.\"\nc E05.3 yes config/policy.yaml:6 \"- ehr__cancel_appointment\" \"Checked policy.yaml and tools.allowlist.yaml: both name tools by manifest server id prefix, and a server not in the manifest is refused (registry.ts:107-111).\" \"Approval and allowlist entries are keyed by verified server id.\"\nit E05 likely_pass medium \"Tools are keyed by manifest server id, with lookalike and duplicate checks across servers.\" \"Register a duplicate server in a test deployment (recipe E05).\"\n# E06\nc E06.1 no src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:56 \"const transport = new StreamableHTTPClientTransport(new URL(server.url), {\" \"\" \"The agent connects straight to the EHR MCP server using per-clinic OAuth secrets it holds (ehr-mcp.ts:36), and NetworkPolicy allows a direct route to the EHR /28 (deployment.yaml:193). There is no separate gateway the agent cannot go around.\"\nc E06.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No gateway exists in the repo, so token checks and downstream credentials cannot be read.\"\nc E06.3 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"The in-process executor authorises and audits each call (executor.ts:55-95), but no separate gateway applies request and response validation or rate limits.\"\nc E06.4 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"Scanner and approval-store errors fail closed in the harness (registry.ts:116, approvals.ts:71), but there is no gateway policy engine to test.\"\nc E06.5 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No gateway routing headers or shared tool-list cache exist; the tool list is read once at start.\"\nc E06.6 unknown src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:38 \"const res = await fetch(token_url, {\" \"\" \"The agent itself requests EHR tokens with client credentials from a URL inside the secret, with no issuer check or address filter on that URL.\"\nit E06 gap medium \"There is no gateway the agent cannot bypass: it connects directly to the EHR MCP server with credentials it holds.\" \"Route MCP traffic through an enforcement gateway that holds the server credentials.\" \"Send MCP calls through a gateway, or a similar enforcement layer, that the agent can't get around.\"\n# E07\nc E07.1 no src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 \"const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));\" \"\" \"The peer's attestation is verified against a key set at a URL named in its own header, so whoever controls the reply controls the signing keys. Only the issuer claim is checked, not the sender's identity.\"\nc E07.2 no src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:90 \"return Eligibility.parse(payload.eligibility);\" \"\" \"The schema is strict, but the attestation is not tied to the clinic, patient or request asked about, and there is no per-peer limit on what it may claim.\"\nc E07.3 no src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:78 \"const rpc = Rpc.parse(JSON.parse(text));\" \"\" \"The reply id is never compared with the request id (line 57-58), and the attestation holds no nonce, so a valid attestation within 5 minutes can be replayed for another patient.\"\nc E07.4 yes src/tools/executor.ts:90 \"return toolResult(call.id, safe);\" \"Traced peer content: Eligibility fields flow only through checkEligibilityForAppointment into a tool_result (executor.ts:174-180, 90); system prompt building (loop.ts:49) takes no peer content.\" \"Peer reply content is returned as tool-result data.\"\nc E07.5 no src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83 \"const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));\" \"\" \"The key-set URL from the peer is fetched with no private, loopback or metadata address check.\"\nfl E07 src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:39 \"A forgeable attestation field (depositWaived) triggers a deposit refund.\"\nit E07 gap high \"The peer reply is verified with keys fetched from a URL the reply itself names, so it is not authenticated.\" \"Pin the eligibility JWKS URL and issuer in config, bind the attestation to the request id, clinic and patient, and block private addresses.\" \"Authenticate the sending agent (prove its identity) on every message, even validly signed ones.\" \"B09\"\n# E08\nc E08.1 yes src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:44 'scope: `eligibility:read clinic:${clinicId} patient:${patientId}`,' \"Checked the only peer call: a per-call RFC 8693 exchange narrows the token to one audience, a read scope, and one clinic and patient (lines 35-50); no spawn or shared credential path exists.\" \"The peer token is narrowed per call.\"\nc E08.2 unknown src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:41 \"subject_token: workloadToken,\" \"\" \"The exchange uses the agent's workload token as subject_token and has no actor_token; the patient appears only in scope. How the peer authorises is outside this repo.\"\nc E08.3 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"The peer's scope is read-only by token (eligibility-a2a.ts:44); the peer's own enforcement is outside this repo.\"\nc E08.4 unknown src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:43 'audience: \"eligibility-agent\",' \"\" \"The audience is set; whether the peer rejects other audiences is outside this repo.\"\nit E08 needs_evidence medium \"The peer token is narrowed per call, but peer-side enforcement and delegated-subject handling are outside this repo.\" \"Test a parent token at the eligibility service and show it is rejected.\"\n# E09\nc E09.1 unknown src/control/kill-switch.ts:70 \"a.abort.abort(new Halted(\" \"\" \"Stop aborts the run's model, tool and peer fetches through the abort signal. A task cancel to the eligibility peer and closing of EHR MCP sessions are not sent.\"\nc E09.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"Workload tokens last 900 s (deployment.yaml:111) and peer tokens are exchanged per call, but stop does not revoke them and peer-side lease behaviour is outside this repo.\"\nc E09.3 yes src/workers/reminders.ts:33 \"await killSwitch.assertRunning(clinic.id);\" \"Searched src/ for queues, schedulers and retry loops: only the cron job, which checks the flag before each clinic and each send (reminders.ts:29,33) and has no retries (deployment.yaml:125).\" \"The reminder job checks the stop flag before each send and does not retry.\"\nc E09.4 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"Completed effects are in the audit trail (tool.executed), but the stop path does not list them for reconciliation.\"\nit E09 needs_evidence medium \"Stop aborts in-flight calls and the cron job checks the flag, but peer cancel, revocation and effect reconciliation are not shown.\" \"Run the E09 drill including the eligibility peer and reconcile completed effects.\"\n# E10\nc E10.1 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"The agent and reminder job write the six fields. The EHR MCP server and eligibility peer are outside this repo.\"\nc E10.2 yes infra/terraform/iam.tf:52 'Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]' \"Read the runtime role: no S3 or Firehose delete and update actions, and the bucket has Object Lock in compliance mode for 7 years (main.tf:139-146).\" \"The runtime role can only append through Firehose.\"\nc E10.3 yes config/tools.allowlist.yaml:6 \"- tool: ehr__find_patient\" \"Read all 11 allowlisted tools; none touches audit storage, logs or retention.\" \"No callable tool can edit audit records.\"\nc E10.4 no src/integrations/payments.ts:37 'metadata: { source: \"clinic-agent\" } ' \"\" \"The refund request tells the vendor only source clinic-agent, not the run or instance id, and tool.executed stores no refund id, SMS message id or EHR receipt (executor.ts:89).\"\nit E10 gap medium \"Vendor calls are not linked in either direction: no run or instance id is sent and vendor receipt ids are not stored.\" \"Send run id and instance id to vendors and store their receipt ids in the audit record.\" \"Check that a vendor boundary doesn't leave any action untraceable to the agent and instance that did it.\"\n# E11\nc E11.1 yes infra/terraform/main.tf:144 \"years = 7\" \"Read the audit bucket lock rule (main.tf:139-147): compliance mode, 7 years.\" \"Audit objects are retained 7 years.\"\nc E11.2 unknown \"\" \"\" \"\" \"No bucket policy or Athena/KMS access rules for reading audit data are in the repo; PHI redaction before audit is not defined for detail fields.\"\nc E11.3 no infra/terraform/main.tf:143 '\"COMPLIANCE\"' \"\" \"Object Lock protects stored objects, but audit events carry no sequence number or chain, and no alert on a delivery gap or Firehose failure is defined.\"\nc E11.4 no src/tools/executor.ts:89 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' \"\" \"The action runs on line 86 and its audit record is written afterwards. A failed audit write after the side effect does not undo it, and the code comment at recorder.ts:69 says the opposite.\"\nit E11 gap high \"Tool actions are audited after they run, so an audit outage does not stop a refund, send or booking.\" \"Write an attempt record first and refuse high-impact actions if it fails.\" \"High-impact actions must fail closed when required audit capture isn't working.\" \"R13\"\nit E12 needs_evidence low \"Code cannot show a fleet incident drill; no runbook or responder routing is in the repo.\" \"Run the E12 drill and name the outside-reporting decision-maker.\"","description":"Record E01-E12 answers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":875,"cache_read_input_tokens":292451,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":875},"output_tokens":96,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be046cb2-a615-4b99-9b5b-9574ded4eee7","uuid":"4791737c-fa27-4cc1-aaf9-d996807d0cda","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:31:07.143Z","request_id":"req_011CfdeeQJp95PW46CdSGQEf","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XVnSWQyGC8iuLZCkdjQeJg":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7 && . ./h.sh\nc E01.3 no src/integrations/payments.ts:9 'const BASE = process.env.PAYMENTS_API ?? \"https://api.payments-provider.example/v2\";' \"\" \"The payments API, SMS API (sms.ts:8), STS (config.ts:62), chat JWKS (config.ts:59) and the Anthropic API are called but are not in release/manifest.json or any other inventory.\"\n# E02\nc E02.1 unknown package.json:17 '\"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",' \"\" \"Direct dependencies and images are pinned exactly, but no package-lock.json is in the tree. The EHR MCP server is a remote vendor service pinned by certificate (manifest.json:42), with no implementation version.\"\nc E02.2 unknown .github/workflows/ci.yml:20 \"- run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\" \"\" \"Image signing and verification exist (ci.yml:73, deploy.yml:66). No npm provenance or signature check is run for packages.\"\nc E02.3 no .github/workflows/ci.yml:22 \"- run: npm test\" \"\" \"ci.yml steps are install, lint, test, build and image; there is no npm audit, osv-scanner, trivy or grype step, and the ECR scan_on_push (main.tf:92) does not gate the build.\"\nc E02.4 no release/manifest.json:43 '\"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"' \"\" \"No approval record names publisher, permissions and update source for each dependency; the manifest has owner and certificate pin for the EHR server only.\"\nit E02 gap medium \"No vulnerability scan gates the build and no dependency approval records exist.\" \"Add an audit or osv scan that fails the build and record publisher, permissions and update source per dependency.\" \"known vulnerabilities\"\n# E03\nc E03.1 no src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 \"c.listTools(),\" \"\" \"Tools are listed from the EHR server and passed to the registry. No hash of an approved tool's description and schema is stored anywhere (searched src/ and release/).\"\nc E03.2 no src/tools/registry.ts:107 \"const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\" \"\" \"registerMcp checks only the server id, then the metadata scan. There is no fingerprint compare on load, refresh or reconnect, and no list_changed handler exists (searched src/).\"\nc E03.3 no src/tools/registry.ts:126 \"for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\" \"\" \"Any tool that passes the text scan is registered with its current definition; a changed description or schema is accepted if it is clean.\"\nc E03.4 no release/manifest.json:42 '\"tlsCertSha256\"' \"\" \"The EHR MCP server is pinned by certificate only. No implementation version or attestation is recorded apart from a metadata fingerprint, and the vendor's code cannot be seen.\"\nfl E03 src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 \"Tool list loaded from the server with no comparison to an approved fingerprint (pre-scan H011).\"\n$PY $S/answer.py $F prescan H011 --verdict=confirmed --item=E03 --reason=\"listTools() results go straight to scanServer and into the registry; no stored fingerprint is compared.\" | head -1 | cut -c1-60\nit E03 gap high \"Tool descriptions and schemas from the EHR server are scanned but never compared with an approved fingerprint.\" \"Store a hash of each approved tool's description and schema and block on mismatch at load, refresh and list-changed.\" \"Take a fingerprint of each approved tool's description and schema.\"\n# E04\nc E04.1 yes src/tools/registry.ts:114 \"scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\" \"Traced every path that loads MCP metadata: server.ts:48-49 is the only caller of registerMcp. Scanned fields: instructions, prompts, resource templates (metadata-scan.ts:100-115), tool name, title, description, input and output schemas and annotations (lines 119-126). Native tools are written in-house (executor.ts:100-183).\" \"All server metadata fields are scanned before tools reach the model.\"\nc E04.2 yes src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:41 \"const RULES: Array<{ rule: string; re: RegExp }> = [\" \"Read the rules (lines 41-58) and LIMITS (33-39): control and invisible characters, role overrides and markers, concealment, precondition injection, base64 and hex blobs, escaped unicode, URLs, emails, phone numbers, references to other servers' tools (line 67-70), and length limits.\" \"The rules cover each required category and length limits.\"\nc E04.3 yes src/tools/registry.ts:123 \"for (const [tool, findings] of scan.rejectedTools) {\" \"Read registry.ts:119-134: a server finding rejects the server, a tool finding rejects only that tool, and only acceptedTools are added.\" \"Flagged tools and servers are rejected, not just logged.\"\nc E04.4 yes src/tools/registry.ts:116 \"metadata scan error\" \"Checked registry.ts:112-118 (error rejects the server) and server.ts:47-52 (catalog failure disables EHR tools); test controls.test.ts:86-92 covers a throwing scanner. No flag turns the scan off.\" \"A scanner error rejects the whole server.\"\nit E04 likely_pass medium \"A metadata scanner covers every field, rejects flagged items, and fails closed on error.\" \"Run poisoned-metadata fixtures against the live server (recipe E04).\"\n# E05\nc E05.1 yes src/tools/registry.ts:128 'key: `${serverId}__${t.name}`,' \"Checked that serverId comes from the manifest id used when the pinned connection is made (server.ts:40-49, ehr-mcp.ts:16-25); reportedName is only logged (registry.ts:109).\" \"Keys are the manifest server id plus tool name.\"\nc E05.2 yes src/tools/registry.ts:151 \"if (editDistanceAtMostOne(canonical(existing.name), c)) {\" \"Read add() (lines 137-158): duplicates and lookalikes (case, digit and rn/vv confusables, edit distance one) across servers are rejected and recorded as conflicts; tests cover them (controls.test.ts:13-45).\" \"Duplicate and lookalike names across servers are flagged and rejected.\"\nc E05.3 yes config/policy.yaml:6 \"- ehr__cancel_appointment\" \"Checked policy.yaml and tools.allowlist.yaml: both name tools by manifest server id prefix, and a server not in the manifest is refused (registry.ts:107-111).\" \"Approval and allowlist entries are keyed by verified server id.\"\nit E05 likely_pass medium \"Tools are keyed by manifest server id, with lookalike and duplicate checks across servers.\" \"Register a duplic