ntext (trace and span IDs) is stored in the audit record itself, not only in separate tracing spans.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check it stores trace and span IDs (or `traceparent`) as fields in the record itself. 3) Answer no if trace context exists only in OpenTelemetry spans, or the record's trace field is never filled.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts:14\",\n          \"quote\": \"traceparent: z.string().regex(\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Checked that every writer spreads ctx.identity() (loop.ts:33, executor.ts:42, reminders.ts:37), which sets traceparent (identity.ts:110).\",\n          \"note\": \"traceparent is a field of the audit record itself.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Tenant and owner values come from the trusted layer, not from baggage, tracestate, or other unprotected headers.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where tenant and owner values for audit records are read. 2) Trace each back to its source: token claims, verified session, IAM tags, or SPIFFE path, versus OTel baggage, `tracestate`, headers like `X-Tenant-Id`, request body, or tool arguments. 3) Answer no if any path takes them from an unprotected source.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/routes/webchat.ts:43\",\n          \"quote\": \"const tenantId = (req.headers[\\\"x-clinic-id\\\"] as string | undefined) ?? claims.clinic_id;\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The audit tenantId comes from RunContext, which the web chat builds from a caller-supplied x-clinic-id header ahead of the verified token claim.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"A04\"\n      ],\n      \"summary