     \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Limits on loop count, run time, tokens, cost, tool-call rate, and number of sub-agents started are set in code or config.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search for `max_turns`, `recursion_limit`, `max_iterations`, `timeout`, `max_tokens`, cost or budget caps, rate limits, sub-agent caps. 2) Check each of the six limits has a value. 3) Answer no if any is missing, set to unlimited (`None`, `0`, `-1`, `inf`), or the loop is `while True` with no cap.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"config/budgets.yaml:3\",\n          \"quote\": \"maxTurns: 8\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched for unlimited values and while(true) loops; loop.ts:55 is for(;;) but budget.turn() at line 56 caps it. All six limits have numbers (turns, wall, tokens, cost, tool rate, peer calls); budgets.yaml:10 states the agent starts no sub-agents.\",\n          \"note\": \"Loop, wall time, token, cost, tool-rate and peer-call limits are set.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The harness or a gateway outside the model enforces each limit and stops or escalates the run when it is hit; the model cannot raise, reset, or skip them.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) For each limit, find the code that enforces it and what happens when hit. 2) Check it runs in the harness or gateway. 3) Answer no if a limit is only in the prompt, can be changed by a tool argument or model output, is caught and the run continues, or hitting it has no stop or escalation.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/budget.ts:102\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (used > max) {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read budget.ts check/shared, loop.ts catch (95-111) and executor.ts:92: BudgetExceeded aborts the signal and stops the run; the limits come from config/budgets.yaml, not the model.\",\n          \"note\": \"The harness throws and aborts when a limit is passed; the run stops and hands off to staff.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Budgets apply to nested sub-agents, so their usage counts against the limits.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find sub-agent spawning (`spawn`, `Task`, `handoff`, `create_agent`). 2) Check child runs share or deduct from the parent budget and depth is capped. 3) Answer no if each child gets a fresh budget, nested spawns are uncounted, or depth and count are unlimited.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"config/budgets.yaml:10\",\n          \"quote\": \"maxPeerCalls: 2\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for spawn, handoff, Task and create_agent; none. The only delegation is the eligibility peer, capped by budget.ts:154-157.\",\n          \"note\": \"No sub-agents exist; peer calls are counted against the run budget.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Spend and rate quotas also apply per user or service, per tenant, and across the fleet, counted across runs, not only within one run.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search gateway, LLM proxy (LiteLLM budgets), and provider config for per-user, per-tenant, and fleet quotas. 2) Check counts persist across runs (shared store, not process memory). 3) Answer no if only per-run limits exist. Answer unknown if quotas would live in a provider console or gateway outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/budget.ts:139\",\n          \"quote\": \"await this.shared(\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Per-subject, per-tenant and fleet quotas are kept in DynamoDB (budget.ts:32-56, 138-162). But the intent classifier call (loop.ts:41) and count_tokens calls are not counted in cost or quotas, and run starts are not rate limited, so many short runs routed to staff use no counted budget. Provider-side spend limits are outside the repo.\"\n        }\n   