 alerts are not in this repo.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Pin the eligibility JWKS URL in config, and show the proxy allowlist, redirect/IP controls and block alerts.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B10\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Pinned, verified image\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Pin the container by digest. Before it runs, check its digest and signature against an approved signing key, or an approved certificate identity and issuer. Keep its build provenance (the record of how it was built) and its list of dependencies. Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build (SLSA `externalParameters`) against what you expect. Keep the verifier patched. Cosign versions before 2.6.2 and 3.0.4 could accept a bundle whose transparency-log entry didn't match the artifact. Confirm that the admission check covers production namespaces and is set to enforce, not just audit. Show that an unapproved or changed image is rejected.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Tool or MCP server package not vetted or pinned\",\n          \"owner\": \"E02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Model weights or adapters loaded without a signature or format check\",\n          \"owner\": \"C05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Image runs as root or includes a shell or package manager\",\n          \"owner\": \"B11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Secrets baked into the image\",\n          \"owner\": \"B03\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 76,\n          \"note\": \"Deployment, CronJob and Dockerfile bases are pinned by digest.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Production manifests reference images by digest (`@sha256:`), not by tag alone.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find every `image:` field in manifests, Helm values, compose, and Terraform. 2) Check each uses `@sha256:`. 3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:76\",\n          \"quote\": \"clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Checked every image: field (Deployment line 76, CronJob line 143) and both Dockerfile FROM lines; all use @sha256.\",\n          \"note\": \"Deployment, CronJob and Dockerfile bases are pinned by digest.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.2\",\n          \"check\": \"An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper). 2) Check the key or certificate identity and issuer are pinned. 3) Answer no if identity or issuer uses `.*` or wildcard regex, issuer is unset, or no admission policy exists. Answer unknown if admission config is outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:67\",\n          \"quote\": \"--certificate-identity\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Signature is verified in the deploy workflow with a pinned identity and issuer (deploy.yml:66-68). No admission policy (Kyverno, policy-controller) is in the repo; the namespace only enforces Pod Security. A cluster-level admission policy may exist outside it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The policy checks provenance fields: builder, source repository, build type, and external parameters.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) In the admission policy, find attestation or provenance conditions. 2) Check builder ID, source repository, build type, and `externalParameters` are each compared to expected values. 3) Answer no if any is missing, provenance is only generated in CI but not verified, or conditions use wildcards.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:66\",\n          \"quote\": \"cosign verify\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Only the signature is verified. Provenance is generated in CI (ci.yml:67) but nothing checks builder, source repo, build type or externalParameters (no verify-attestation).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.4\",\n          \"check\": \"The policy is in enforce mode, covers production namespaces, and denies images that match no policy.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Read the policy mode and scope (`validationFailureAction`, `failureAction`, `mode`, namespace selectors, exclusions). 2) Check for a no-match deny. 3) Answer no if mode is `Audit` or `warn`, production namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No admission policy in the repo, so mode, namespace scope and no-match deny cannot be read.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.5\",\n          \"check\": \"The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml:71\",\n          \"quote\": \"cosign-release: v2.6.2\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Both pins checked: ci.yml:71 and deploy.yml:60 are v2.6.2; no other cosign install.\",\n          \"note\": \"Cosign is pinned at 2.6.2 in CI and deploy.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Deploy checks the image signature but never checks build provenance fields, and no admission policy is in the repo.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Add cosign verify-attestation for builder, source repo, build type and externalParameters, and an enforcing admission policy.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Minimal, isolated runtime\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Remove shells, downloaders, package managers, mounts, and privileges the agent doesn't need. As a container baseline, meet the Kubernetes Pod Security Standards \\\"restricted\\\" profile or the same controls elsewhere. That means non-root, no privilege escalation, all capabilities dropped, and a seccomp profile set. Where supported, also use a read-only root filesystem and user namespaces; the restricted profile doesn't require those two. For running untrusted code, use a sandbox that fits the threat, such as a microVM or a user-space kernel. Ordinary containers share the host's kernel. For managed runtimes, record the provider's isolation evidence and what you can't see. Test that host access is blocked. A blocked probe does not prove the sandbox resists every escape.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked\",\n          \"owner\": \"B10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Outbound