e owner on the agent team and the owner on the shared platform or vendor side\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The dependency inventory omits several called services and does not split owners between the agent team and the platform or vendor.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Extend the manifest with every called service and both owners.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"governance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"E02\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Vet and pin dependencies\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Before approving a tool or server, review its source code or available provenance, publisher, permissions, update path, and known vulnerabilities. Include model files, adapters, and datasets. Pin versions or digests, and verify signatures where they exist. A registry's namespace check shows who controls a publisher account, not that the code is safe. Record the limits of remote services and unsigned artifacts, and the extra checks you use instead.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A tool's description or schema changing after it was approved\",\n          \"owner\": \"E03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Hidden instructions inside a tool's metadata\",\n          \"owner\": \"E04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Lookalike or duplicate tool names across servers\",\n          \"owner\": \"E05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked\",\n          \"owner\": \"B10\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml\",\n          \"line\": 22,\n          \"note\": \"ci.yml steps are install, lint, test, build and image; there is no npm audit, osv-scanner, trivy or grype step, and the ECR scan_on_push (main.tf:92) does not gate the build.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {