s, annotations, prompt and resource templates. 3) Answer no if any field, or a second load path, skips the scanner.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/registry.ts:114\",\n          \"quote\": \"scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Traced every path that loads MCP metadata: server.ts:48-49 is the only caller of registerMcp. Scanned fields: instructions, prompts, resource templates (metadata-scan.ts:100-115), tool name, title, description, input and output schemas and annotations (lines 119-126). Native tools are written in-house (executor.ts:100-183).\",\n          \"note\": \"All server metadata fields are scanned before tools reach the model.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E04.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the scanner rules. 2) Check for each: hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters (zero-width, bidi), role overrides, encoded payloads (base64), data-sending targets (URLs, emails), and length limits. 3) Answer no if any one is missing.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:41\",\n          \"quote\": \"const RULES: Array<{ rule: string; re: RegExp }> = [\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read the rules (lines 41-58) and LIMITS (33-39): control and invisible characters, role overrides and markers, concealment, precondition injection, base64 and hex blobs, escaped unicode, URLs, emails, phone numbers, references to other servers' tools (line 67-70), and length limits.\",\n          \"note\": \"The rules cover each required category and length limits.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E04.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Metadata