l tool results by source, gate ungated writes and sends in code, and run repeated adaptive injection tests.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"security\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R03\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Prevent output and log leakage\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Remove secrets and limit sensitive data before tool output, debug output, or responses reach the model, outside recipients, or normal logs. Some clients fetch URLs on their own when they display output, such as Markdown images and link previews. These can leak data without any tool call, so block them or allow only approved URLs. Check generated output before it goes into SQL, a shell, an HTML page, or anything else that runs it. Use parameterized queries and commands (for example, argument lists for shell calls), and the right escaping for each context. Test with fake secrets and injection payloads. Confirm that leaks and unintended execution are blocked, and that redacted audit evidence is kept.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A tool call sending data to an unapproved destination\",\n          \"owner\": \"B09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Long-lived secrets checked into config or baked into images\",\n          \"owner\": \"B03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Incoming hostile payloads not validated\",\n          \"owner\": \"R01\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Retrieval returning another tenant's documents\",\n          \"owner\": \"R04\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/tools/executor.ts\",\n          \"line\": 87,\n          \"note\": \"The raw EHR/payments/SMS result is logged at info before redactPhi runs on the next lines. Contact lookups return phone numbers and names. Replies to patients (loop.ts:79-85) also pass through no redaction.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"chec