hange index content, and the ingestion path checks the writer.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find index write paths (`upsert`, `add_documents`, `index`, ingestion jobs). 2) Check each verifies the writer identity or source against a named list. 3) Answer no if any write path, including the agent's own tools or an admin endpoint, accepts writes without that check.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:51\",\n          \"quote\": \"const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for vector stores, embeddings, retrievers, document loaders and index writes; none. Messages are built from the patient text only.\",\n          \"note\": \"There is no index, so no write path exists to check.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R04.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Each stored chunk has metadata for source, time added, trust level, and access permissions.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find chunk write code and metadata fields. 2) Check source, time added, trust level, and access permissions are stored on every chunk. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or set only on some ingestion paths.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No retrieval corpus or index exists, so chunk metadata does not apply.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R04.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Search applies the requesting tenant's access filter at query time, in the store or retrieval code, not after the model answers.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find search calls (`similarity_search`, `query`, `search`, `filter=`, `where=`). 2) Check a tenant or access filter is applied in the store query, from the caller's identity. 3) Answer no if filtering happens after retrieval or in the prompt, the filter is optional, or the tenant comes from a model-supplied argument.\",\n          \"met\": \"