o remove it\",\n          \"owner\": \"R06\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Retrieval search not filtered by the requesting tenant\",\n          \"owner\": \"R04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent credentials allowing another tenant's data at the API\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Rollback restoring old memory or index state unchecked\",\n          \"owner\": \"C07\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"na_candidate\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/agent/loop.ts\",\n          \"line\": 51,\n          \"note\": \"Nothing persists between runs, so no memory scope exists to check.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Memory reads and writes are scoped by tenant, agent type, instance, and task as needed, and cross-scope access is denied unless explicitly allowed.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find memory read and write code (`memory`, `store`, `namespace`, keys). 2) Check keys include tenant, agent type, instance, or task as needed. 3) Answer no if keys omit tenant, the scope comes from a model argument, or reads fall back to a shared or global namespace.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:51\",\n          \"quote\": \"const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for memory stores, session or thread state and saved summaries; none. Every run starts from the patient message and the EHR.\",\n          \"note\": \"Nothing persists between runs, so no memory scope exists to check.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R05.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Every memory write, including content arriving through ordinary queries, passes validation before it is stored.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) List every memory write path, including automatic saves from ordinary conversation. 2) Check each passes validation before storing. 3) Answer no if any path writes without validation, or validation errors are caught and the write continues.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No memory persists between runs (README.md:26, release/manifest.json:61); runs keep no state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R05.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The agent's own output cannot reach trusted or shared memory without a review step.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where agent output is written to shared or trusted memory. 2) Check a review step gates the write. 3) Answer no if agent output goes straight into shared or trusted memory, or the review flag defaults to approved.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No memory persists between runs (README.md:26, release/manifest.json:61); runs keep no state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R05.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Unverified entries have an expiry that is enforced.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find how unverified entries are marked and expired (`ttl`, `expires_at`, cleanup jobs). 2) Check reads filter out expired entries. 3) Answer no if no expiry is set, it is set but never enforced on read or by a job, or the default is no expiry.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No memory persists between runs (README.md:26, release/manifest.json:61); runs keep no state.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The agent keeps no memory between runs.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Governance to approve N/A; confirm no state is added