n.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find restart logic (supervisors, `restartPolicy`, cron, auto-resume). 2) Answer no if a stopped run restarts automatically (`restartPolicy: Always`, auto-resume from checkpoint) without an operator action.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:133\",\n          \"quote\": \"restartPolicy: Never\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Runs keep no checkpoint or queue (README.md:26) and the cron job never restarts (line 133, backoffLimit 0); pods restarting only start a fresh server.\",\n          \"note\": \"A stopped run is not resumed; new runs check the stop flag.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R12.5\",\n          \"check\": \"Workers and queued jobs lose their credentials or authority at stop, so no orphaned work can act.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find workers and queued jobs and the credentials they hold. 2) Check stop revokes or expires them. 3) Answer no if workers keep long-lived credentials after stop, or jobs carry their own tokens that stay valid.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No workers or queued jobs hold their own tokens; pods keep IRSA credentials until the platform revokes the role.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Where you can't cancel something, show how you check and fix the result (reconcile)\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"No per-operation stop policy or tracked hold exists for outside effects that may have happened when the stop arrived.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Record per operation whether it is cancelled, completed or reconciled, and mark unknown outcomes for operator review.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Full execution audit\",\n      \"requirement