"check\": \"Tool errors, timeouts, and retries are recorded, and each operation gets an ID before it is sent, so unclear results can be matched to the destination's records.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find error, timeout, and retry handling. 2) Check each is logged and each operation gets an ID before sending. 3) Answer no if `except`/`catch` blocks skip logging, retries are not logged, or the ID is created after the response.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:93\",\n          \"quote\": \"await audit.record({ ...base, event: \\\"tool.failed\\\", approvalId, reason: (err as Error).message.slice(0, 300) });\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Failures are recorded, but SDK retries are not, a timeout is logged like any failure with no unknown-outcome marker, and the tool-use id is the only operation id sent (refunds add an idempotency key, SMS and EHR writes do not).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R13.5\",\n          \"check\": \"Records are written by the harness or gateway, not by the model, and do not depend on the run's final answer.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find who writes records. 2) Answer no if the model writes them via a tool, records are built from the final answer, or logging runs only if the run completes.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:51\",\n          \"quote\": \"await audit.record({ ...base, event: \\\"tool.denied\\\", reason });\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Checked the allowlist (no audit tool exists) and the run flow: records are written by loop.ts and executor.ts, and run.stopped is written in the catch (loop.ts:107), not from the final answer.\",\n          \"note\": \"The harness writes audit records, including on denial and failure.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [\n        \"src/tools/executor.ts:86 The tool runs (line 86) before the tool.executed audit (line 89); if the audit write fails, AuditUnavailable is rethrown (line 92) after a side effect already happened, so the action is unrecorded.\"\n      ],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"authorization decisions with the policy version used\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"E11\",\n        \"R01\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Executed actions are logged without arguments, results or policy version, and after the action runs.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Fix policy.version, add key arguments and results, and write an attempt record before the call.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R14\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Recovery integrity\",\n      \"requirement\": \"If logs or checkpoints drive recovery, make them tamper-evident. Before using them, verify them against a separately protected trust anchor or signing key. Test that verification rejects changed checkpoints. It must also catch truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of a whole hash chain. For automatic recovery, confirm the destination supports idempotency: sending the same request twice has the effect of sending it once. Replay only within the destination's documented scope and time window. Confirm that actions you can't undo don't happen twice. Where support is missing or the result is unclear, check that replay pauses for reconciliation instead of sending again.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"What happens to in-flight writes and queued actions at stop\",\n          \"owner\": \"R12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Rollback to an approved earlier release not tested\",\n          \"owner\": \"C07\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent able to delete or rewrite its own audit history\",\n          \"owner\": \"E10\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"na_candidate\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/agent/loop.ts\",\n          \"line\": 51,\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoint or recovery log drives recovery.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Checkpoints and audit records used for recovery are hash-chained or signed.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find checkpoint and audit storage used for recovery. 2) Check for hash chaining or signatures. 3) Answer no if records are plain rows or files with no chain or signature.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:51\",\n          \"quote\": \"const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for checkpoints, resume, replay and recovery code; none. Retries are the SDK's maxRetries 1 (loop.ts:15) and a provider idempotency key on refunds.\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoint or recovery log drives recovery.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Recovery verifies them against a key or trust anchor stored separately from the records, and refuses any that fail.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find recovery code that loads checkpoints. 2) Check it verifies against a key stored separately and refuses failures. 3) Answer no if the key sits in the same store, verification is skipped, or failure is logged and recovery continues.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Verification catches truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of the whole chain, for example with a signed head or sequence number held outside the store.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Check verification uses a signed head or sequence number held outside the store. 2) Answer no if truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, or replacing the whole chain would still pass.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Automatic replay sends idempotency keys that the destination enforces, and only for integrations that support them.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find replay code. 2) Check it sends idempotency keys (`Idempotency-Key`, `client_token`) only to integrations that enforce them. 3) Answer no if replay sends without keys, uses a local dedupe table as the only guard, or replays to integrations without support.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.5\",\n          \"check\": \"When idempotency is missing or the result is unclear, replay pauses for reconciliation instead of resending.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find replay handling for unclear results or missing idempotency. 2) Answer no if replay resends instead of pausing for reconciliation, or retry is the default on timeout.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"No checkpoints or automatic replay exist; runs start fresh.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Governance to approve N/A; confirm SDK retries are the only retry.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"injection_attempts\": [],\n  \"prescan_resolutions\": {\n    \"H006\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Run-start audit (loop.ts:36) precedes the try; audit failures in the try throw AuditUnavailable to the catch and stop the run before any tool runs, and error and stop paths also write records (loop.ts:107).\"\n    },\n    \"H007\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Same block as H006: intent.classified is audited before routing and a failure stops the run; nothing proceeds on an audit error.\"\n    },\n    \"H008\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"This writes run.stopped while the run is already stopping; a failure is logged with the reason and no action proceeds.\"\n    },\n    \"H009\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"reason\": \"executeTool runs tool.invoke (line 86) before the tool.executed audit (line 89), so an audit outage after the side effect leaves it unrecorded.\"\n    },\n    \"H010\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n      \"item\": \"R13\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same try block: success is audited only after the action; the catch rethrows AuditUnavailable (line 92).\"\n    },\n    \"H011\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n      \"item\": \"E03\",\n      \"reason\": \"listTools() results go straight to scanServer and into the registry; no stored fingerprint is compared.\"\n    },\n    \"H001\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Pod-level context sets runAsNonRoot true and seccomp RuntimeDefault; the container context below it sets the rest, and the namespace enforces restricted.\"\n    },\n    \"H002\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Container context sets allowPrivilegeEscalation false, readOnlyRootFilesystem true, drop ALL, and inherits non-root and seccomp from the pod.\"\n    },\n    \"H003\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"CronJob pod context sets runAsNonRoot true and seccomp RuntimeDefault for its single container.\"\n    },\n    \"H004\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"CronJob container sets allowPrivilegeEscalation false, readOnlyRootFilesystem true and drop ALL; non-root and seccomp come from the pod.\"\n    },\n    \"H005\": {\n      \"verdict\": \"dismissed\",\n      \"item\": null,\n      \"reason\": \"Resource star is on ecr:GetAuthorizationToken in the GitHub deploy role (github.tf:91-101), which needs it; it is not attached to the agent runtime identity.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":9,"newStart":1,"newLines":9,"lines":[" {","   \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",","-  \"repo\": \"\",","+  \"repo\": \"agent/ (clinic-agent, Northbay Clinic Group scheduling agent; not a git repository)\",","   \"commit\": null,","   \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T15:19:03Z\",","-  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",","+  \"scope\": \"Read-only review of every file under agent/ (src, config, prompts, release manifest, Dockerfile, k8s, Terraform, GitHub workflows and CODEOWNERS, tests, README) against all 53 BRACE items, with the pre-scan (11 hits, all resolved). Found: agent loop (src/agent/loop.ts), tool executor and registry (src/tools), EHR MCP client, payments, SMS, A2A eligibility peer, kill switch, audit recorder, reminder cron job, web chat and SMS routes. Not found in the repo: .brace/ record, MCP gateway, admission policy, drift detector, security detection rules or alert routing, rollback runbook, package-lock.json, retrieval or memory store, sub-agents. Not examined: the staff approval console, the platform egress proxy, the EHR vendor server, the eligibility peer, SSO and IAM outside Terraform, and the live deployment. Nothing was run. Reviewed by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) in normal mode (no --conservative flag). Challenge steps (step 8) were NOT performed here: every likely_pass and G1/G2 na_candidate rating is unchallenged and the hunt has not run. Eight likely_pass items (A01, A07, B08, B11, B12, C02, E04, E05, R07 are nine; see list) and the N/A candidates R04 and R14 await fresh challengers.\",","   \"findings\": [","     {","       \"item\": \"A01\","]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true}}
