{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QiLcLyJYgJiDWxqfHkrkL3","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7/agent/brace-findings.json has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"be046cb2-a615-4b99-9b5b-9574ded4eee7","uuid":"455d7a5f-73ca-4006-b4d0-930d6edda6c3","timestamp":"2026-10-02T15:32:25.303Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-repeat-_3kdytd7/agent/brace-findings.json","oldString":"Eight likely_pass items (A01, A07, B08, B11, B12, C02, E04, E05, R07 are nine; see list) and the N/A candidates R04 and R14 await fresh challengers.","newString":"Nine likely_pass items (A01, A07, B08, B11, B12, C02, E04, E05, R07) and the G1/G2 N/A candidates R04 and R14 await fresh challengers.","originalFile":"{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"agent/ (clinic-agent, Northbay Clinic Group scheduling agent; not a git repository)\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-02T15:19:03Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Read-only review of every file under agent/ (src, config, prompts, release manifest, Dockerfile, k8s, Terraform, GitHub workflows and CODEOWNERS, tests, README) against all 53 BRACE items, with the pre-scan (11 hits, all resolved). Found: agent loop (src/agent/loop.ts), tool executor and registry (src/tools), EHR MCP client, payments, SMS, A2A eligibility peer, kill switch, audit recorder, reminder cron job, web chat and SMS routes. Not found in the repo: .brace/ record, MCP gateway, admission policy, drift detector, security detection rules or alert routing, rollback runbook, package-lock.json, retrieval or memory store, sub-agents. Not examined: the staff approval console, the platform egress proxy, the EHR vendor server, the eligibility peer, SSO and IAM outside Terraform, and the live deployment. Nothing was run. Reviewed by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) in normal mode (no --conservative flag). Challenge steps (step 8) were NOT performed here: every likely_pass and G1/G2 na_candidate rating is unchallenged and the hunt has not run. Eight likely_pass items (A01, A07, B08, B11, B12, C02, E04, E05, R07 are nine; see list) and the N/A candidates R04 and R14 await fresh challengers.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A01\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Distinct agent identity\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Give the agent its own non-human identity. Keep it separate from the user who launched it and from unrelated agents. Show that permissions and revocation belong to that identity, even when a user starts the run.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Instance or tenant labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A credential scoped to more operations, resources, or tenants than needed\",\n          \"owner\": \"B02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Revocation delay from cached or self-contained tokens not measured\",\n          \"owner\": \"B04\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"likely_pass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 60,\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account bound to the clinic-agent-runtime IAM role.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The agent runs under its own workload principal (service account, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID) that no other service or unrelated agent uses.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the agent's identity: pod `serviceAccountName`, IAM role, SPIFFE ID, or agent ID in IaC or deploy config. 2) Search other deployments, services, and agents in the repo for the same name or role. 3) Answer no if it is shared, `default`, the main backend's identity, or only a string label with no credential. Answer unknown if identity is assigned outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:60\",\n          \"quote\": \"serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched the repo for other uses of this service account and role: only the agent pods and its own reminder CronJob (line 131, same role at line 27) use them; there is no default or shared backend identity.\",\n          \"note\": \"Dedicated service account bound to the clinic-agent-runtime IAM role.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Tool and API clients get credentials from the agent's own principal, not from the launching user's forwarded token or session cookie.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find every place tool and API clients get a token or key. 2) Trace where each comes from: workload identity or token exchange, versus the incoming request's `Authorization` header or session cookie. 3) Check every client, not just the main one. 4) Answer no if any client forwards the user's token or cookie as-is, or uses a shared static key.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:41\",\n          \"quote\": \"subject_token: workloadToken,\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for the request Authorization header being forwarded; webchat.ts:23-33 only verifies it. EHR, payments and SMS use per-clinic secrets from Secrets Manager (ehr-mcp.ts:36, payments.ts:12, sms.ts:23).\",\n          \"note\": \"Clients use the agent's own workload token or service secrets.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.3\",\n          \"check\": \"When a user starts a run, the user is carried as a delegated subject (for example a token exchange with separate act and sub), while the agent keeps its own principal.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the code that starts a run for a user. 2) Look for token exchange (RFC 8693, `subject_token`, `actor_token`, `act`/`sub` claims) or a separate delegated-subject field. 3) Check the agent's own principal is still the actor. 4) Answer no if the user's token is used directly or the user replaces the agent identity. Answer unknown if the exchange happens in an outside identity service.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/tools/executor.ts:44\",\n          \"quote\": \"subject: ctx.subject,\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read identity.ts:56-59 and the audit writer: the user is carried as subject (patient, staff or system) next to the agent's own identity fields. The eligibility exchange keeps the workload token as subject_token and puts clinic and patient in scope (eligibility-a2a.ts:39-45).\",\n          \"note\": \"The user is carried as a separate subject on every action; the agent stays the actor.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A01.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Permissions are bound to the agent principal in IaC or RBAC, so revoking that principal alone removes the agent's access without disabling the user.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find IAM policies, RoleBindings, or grants in Terraform, Helm, or Kubernetes YAML. 2) Check they bind to the agent principal, not to a user, group, or shared role. 3) Check that removing that binding alone would cut the agent's access. 4) Answer no if access depends on the user's grants or a shared credential. Answer unknown if permissions are not defined in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"infra/terraform/iam.tf:25\",\n          \"quote\": \"resource \\\"aws_iam_role_policy\\\" \\\"runtime\\\" {\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read iam.tf:3-57: the policy is attached to role clinic-agent-runtime, assumable only by the two agent service accounts (lines 14-17); no user or group grant is involved.\",\n          \"note\": \"Permissions are bound to the agent role, which can be removed alone.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"The agent has its own service account and IAM role, and users are carried only as a subject.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Run the A01 revocation drill.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A02\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"All six identity fields\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Check that every action records the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context. Look at successful, denied, failed, and background actions, not just the main request path.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Identity labels taken from what the model supplies\",\n          \"owner\": \"A04\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent-type-id not computed as a hash of its identity inputs\",\n          \"owner\": \"A03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent able to erase or rewrite its own audit history\",\n          \"owner\": \"E10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Sub-agent record missing its parent link or parent prompt\",\n          \"owner\": \"A06\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts\",\n          \"line\": 8,\n          \"note\": \"All six fields are required by the audit schema.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.1\",\n          \"check\": \"The audit record schema has all six fields: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, agent-type-id, agent-instance-id, and trace context.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find the audit record schema or the function that writes audit entries. 2) Check for each of the six: accountable party, operational owner, tenant, `agent.type.id`, `agent.instance.id`, trace context (`traceparent` or trace and span IDs). 3) Answer no if any one is missing from the schema or never set.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/audit/recorder.ts:8\",\n          \"quote\": \"export const IdentityFields = z.object({\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read the schema (recorder.ts:8-15): accountableParty, operationalOwner, tenantId, agentTypeId, agentInstanceId and traceparent are all required and validated before any send (line 60).\",\n          \"note\": \"All six fields are required by the audit schema.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.2\",\n          \"check\": \"All six fields are written on denied, failed, async, and background actions too, not only on the successful main request path.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) List every path that writes an audit record, or should: success, policy deny, `except`/`catch` blocks, retries, queue workers, cron jobs, webhooks, other endpoints such as approvals, and refusals before the run starts (quota, rate limit, auth) that return an error without logging. 2) For each, check all six fields are set, ideally by one shared wrapper. 3) Answer no if any deny, error, async, or background path writes records without them, or writes no record at all.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/routes/sms-webhook.ts:57\",\n          \"quote\": \"if (!parsed.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: \\\"invalid payload\\\" });\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Refusals before a run starts write no record: invalid SMS payload (line 57), unknown number (61), and the web chat 401, 400 and 404 returns (webchat.ts:24,36,40,45). Run, tool, denied, failed and reminder paths do carry all six fields.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A02.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Trace context 