s passed; the run stops and hands off to staff.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Budgets apply to nested sub-agents, so their usage counts against the limits.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find sub-agent spawning (`spawn`, `Task`, `handoff`, `create_agent`). 2) Check child runs share or deduct from the parent budget and depth is capped. 3) Answer no if each child gets a fresh budget, nested spawns are uncounted, or depth and count are unlimited.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"config/budgets.yaml:10\",\n          \"quote\": \"maxPeerCalls: 2\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for spawn, handoff, Task and create_agent; none. The only delegation is the eligibility peer, capped by budget.ts:154-157.\",\n          \"note\": \"No sub-agents exist; peer calls are counted against the run budget.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B07.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Spend and rate quotas also apply per user or service, per tenant, and across the fleet, counted across runs, not only within one run.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Search gateway, LLM proxy (LiteLLM budgets), and provider config for per-user, per-tenant, and fleet quotas. 2) Check counts persist across runs (shared store, not process memory). 3) Answer no if only per-run limits exist. Answer unknown if quotas would live in a provider console or gateway outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/agent/budget.ts:139\",\n          \"quote\": \"await this.shared(\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Per-subject, per-tenant and fleet quotas are kept in DynamoDB (budget.ts:32-56, 138-162). But the intent classifier call (loop.ts:41) and count_tokens calls are not counted in cost or quotas, and run starts are not rate limited, so many short runs routed to staff use no counted budget. Provider-side spend limits are outside the repo.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Per-run and shared quotas are enforced in code, but classifier calls and run starts are outside the counted budget.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Count classifier spend in RunBudget or add a per-subject run-rate limit, then drill each limit.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B08\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Environment isolation\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Write down every system and data store the agent can reach. Test that it has no path to unapproved production resources, admin systems, host services, or other tenants. Enforce this in the infrastructure, not only in the prompt. For each allowed connection, also check input and response validation under R01\\u2013R02, including API responses and messages from connected services. Being allowed on the network does not make their content trusted.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Outbound traffic to unapproved internet destinations\",\n          \"owner\": \"B09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Container running as root or shipping a shell it doesn't need\",\n          \"owner\": \"B11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Content from an allowed service trusted without validation\",\n          \"owner\": \"R01\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent reaching an approved MCP server directly instead of through the gateway\",\n          \"owner\": \"E06\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"likely_pass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 168,\n          \"note\": \"Default-deny egress and ingress with named allowed peers.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B08.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Network policy or security groups default-deny and allow only the listed systems and data stores the agent needs.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find NetworkPolicy, security groups, firewall rules, docker-compose networks. 2) Check for a default deny and named allowed peers. 3) Answer no if the agent's namespace has no policy, rules allow all, `0.0.0.0/0` or a broad CIDR is allowed, or allowed peers go beyond the listed systems. Answer unknown if network config lives outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:168\",\n          \"quote\": \"podSelector: {}\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read the whole NetworkPolicy: policyTypes Egress and Ingress with podSelector {} selects every pod; egress allows only kube-dns, the platform egress proxy on 3128 and 10.60.12.0/28:443; ingress only from the ingress namespace on 8080. No other policy in the repo widens it.\",\n          \"note\": \"Default-deny egress and ingress with named allowed peers.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B08.2\",\n          \"check\": \"No route, mount, or credential gives the runtime a path to unapproved production resources, admin systems, host services, or other tenants. Egress to 0.0.0.0/0 or another broad range, even only on ports 80 and 443, is such a route: it reaches cloud metadata (169.254.169.254) and internal services unless they are explicitly blocked.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) List routes, mounts, and credentials in the agent's runtime (egress rules, volumes, env secrets, `hostNetwork`, `docker.sock`). 2) Check each reaches only approved systems. 3) Answer no if egress allows `0.0.0.0/0` or a broad range on any port without blocking 169.254.169.254, if host services or the Docker socket are reachable, or credentials reach production admin or other tenants.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:63\",\n          \"quote\": \"hostNetwork: false\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched manifests for 0.0.0.0/0, hostPath, docker.sock, hostPID: none. Node metadata uses IMDSv2 with hop limit 1 (main.tf:68-69). The routes are the proxy and the EHR /28; what the proxy allows is outside this repo (see B09).\",\n          \"note\": \"No broad egress, host mounts or host namespaces.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B08.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Isolation is enforced in infrastructure config, not by the prompt or by agent code the model can influence.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where isolation is defined. 2) Check it is in infrastructure (NetworkPolicy, VPC, IAM, separate namespace or account). 3) Answer no if it relies on prompt text or agent code (URL checks, host lists in the harness) that the model's output can steer, with no infrastructure rule behind it.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:169\",\n          \"quote\": \"policyTypes: [\\\"Egress\\\", \\\"Ingress\\\"]\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Searched src/ for URL or host checks that would stand in for isolation; none are relied on. Isolation is NetworkPolicy plus IRSA.\",\n          \"note\": \"Isolation is in NetworkPolicy and IAM, not prompt or harness code.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Namespace-wide default-deny NetworkPolicy limits egress to DNS, the egress proxy and the EHR private link.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Keep the proxy allowlist under review (B09).\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B09\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Egress allowlist\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Allow only the outside destinations the task needs. Test a blocked destination and ways around the block, such as going straight past a proxy or gateway. Cover redirects, DNS changes and rebinding, IPv4 and IPv6, and cloud metadata or loopback addresses where they apply. An allowed domain can still host an attacker's account or receive leaked data. So also limit which resources and tenants the agent can reach, and what data it can send. Record each block and confirm the right operator hears about it.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Data leaking through client-side Markdown images or link previews\",\n          \"owner\": \"R03\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Network path to internal production or admin systems\",\n          \"owner\": \"B08\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"A loosened egress rule in the running setup raising no alert\",\n          \"owner\": \"C04\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 193,\n          \"note\": \"Direct routes around the proxy are blocked by NetworkPolicy, not only by env vars.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B09.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Outbound traffic is default-deny, with a destination allowlist enforced at a proxy, gateway, or network policy.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find egress rules (NetworkPolicy egress, Cilium FQDN, proxy ACLs, cloud firewall). 2) Check outbound is default deny with a destination allowlist. 3) Answer no if egress allows `0.0.0.0/0` or broad CIDRs, no egress rules exist, or the allowlist is only in app code the agent runs. Answer unknown if egress is set outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:189\",\n          \"quote\": \"app: egress-proxy\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"NetworkPolicy is default-deny and allows only DNS, the platform egress proxy and the EHR /28. The destination allowlist itself lives in the platform proxy, outside this repo (deployment.yaml:160-161 only describes it).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B09.2\",\n          \"check\": \"Network policy blocks direct routes around the proxy or gateway, for both IPv4 and IPv6.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Check whether the proxy is enforced by network policy or only by `HTTP_PROXY`/`HTTPS_PROXY` env. 2) Check IPv6 egress rules. 3) Answer no if pods can reach the internet except via the proxy, the proxy is only an env var, `NO_PROXY` is broad, or IPv6 is not restricted.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:193\",\n          \"quote\": \"ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read all egress rules: the only IP block is a private /28, no IPv6 range or 0.0.0.0/0, so IPv4 and IPv6 direct routes are denied by default. HTTPS_PROXY (deployment.yaml:43) is only a hint; NO_PROXY (line 44) lists the EHR host and .svc.cluster.local, which the policy still blocks except the EHR /28.\",\n          \"note\": \"Direct routes around the proxy are blocked by NetworkPolicy, not only by env vars.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B09.3\",\n          \"check\": \"Redirect targets and resolved IP addresses are checked against the allowlist, and cloud metadata and loopback addresses are blocked.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find fetch and HTTP client code (`requests`, `fetch`, `http.Client`, `follow_redirects`, `allow_redirects`). 2) Check each redirect hop and resolved IP is checked. 3) Answer no if redirects are followed unchecked, the check uses the hostname but not the resolved IP, or 169.254.169.254, fd00:ec2::254, or 127.0.0.0/8 and ::1 are not blocked.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \"src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:83\",\n          \"quote\": \"const keys = createRemoteJWKSet(new URL(header.jku));\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"The app fetches a key-set URL taken from the peer's own response header, with no host allowlist, redirect check, or private/metadata address check. Other fetches use configured hosts (fetch follows redirects by default). Any filtering would be in the proxy outside this repo.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B09.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Allowed destinations are limited by resource, tenant, or path where needed, not only by domain.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) List allowed destinations that are shared services (S3, GitHub, storage, paste sites). 2) Check rules limit bucket, account, repo, tenant, or path. 3) Answer no if a shared service is allowed by domain or wildcard (`*.s3.amazonaws.com`) alone, or path checks use string prefix without normalising.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Allowed shared services (AWS endpoints, Anthropic, payments, SMS) are listed only in a comment (deployment.yaml:160-162); resource or tenant limits on them would be in the proxy outside this repo.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B09.5\",\n          \"check\": \"Each blocked request is logged and routed as an alert to a named operator.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find where blocked requests are logged (proxy deny log, policy audit, app code). 2) Find the alert route to a named operator. 3) Answer no if blocks are not logged, only allowed requests are logged, or no alert route names an operator. Answer unknown if alerting lives outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Block logging and alert routing for denied egress would be in the proxy and platform alerting; none is in this repo.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Allow only the outside destinations the task needs.\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"E07\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The app fetches a peer-chosen key-set URL, and the destination allowlist and block alerts are not in this repo.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Pin the eligibility JWKS URL in config, and show the proxy allowlist, redirect/IP controls and block alerts.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B10\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Pinned, verified image\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Pin the container by digest. Before it runs, check its digest and signature against an approved signing key, or an approved certificate identity and issuer. Keep its build provenance (the record of how it was built) and its list of dependencies. Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build (SLSA `externalParameters`) against what you expect. Keep the verifier patched. Cosign versions before 2.6.2 and 3.0.4 could accept a bundle whose transparency-log entry didn't match the artifact. Confirm that the admission check covers production namespaces and is set to enforce, not just audit. Show that an unapproved or changed image is rejected.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Tool or MCP server package not vetted or pinned\",\n          \"owner\": \"E02\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Model weights or adapters loaded without a signature or format check\",\n          \"owner\": \"C05\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Image runs as root or includes a shell or package manager\",\n          \"owner\": \"B11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Secrets baked into the image\",\n          \"owner\": \"B03\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"gap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 76,\n          \"note\": \"Deployment, CronJob and Dockerfile bases are pinned by digest.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Production manifests reference images by digest (`@sha256:`), not by tag alone.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find every `image:` field in manifests, Helm values, compose, and Terraform. 2) Check each uses `@sha256:`. 3) Answer no if any production image uses only a tag (`:latest`, `:v1`), or a template defaults to a tag when the digest value is empty.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:76\",\n          \"quote\": \"clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Checked every image: field (Deployment line 76, CronJob line 143) and both Dockerfile FROM lines; all use @sha256.\",\n          \"note\": \"Deployment, CronJob and Dockerfile bases are pinned by digest.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.2\",\n          \"check\": \"An admission policy verifies the signature against a pinned key, or a pinned certificate identity and issuer, with no wildcard identity or issuer.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find admission policies (Kyverno `verifyImages`, `ClusterImagePolicy`, Gatekeeper). 2) Check the key or certificate identity and issuer are pinned. 3) Answer no if identity or issuer uses `.*` or wildcard regex, issuer is unset, or no admission policy exists. Answer unknown if admission config is outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:67\",\n          \"quote\": \"--certificate-identity\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Signature is verified in the deploy workflow with a pinned identity and issuer (deploy.yml:66-68). No admission policy (Kyverno, policy-controller) is in the repo; the namespace only enforces Pod Security. A cluster-level admission policy may exist outside it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.3\",\n          \"check\": \"The policy checks provenance fields: builder, source repository, build type, and external parameters.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) In the admission policy, find attestation or provenance conditions. 2) Check builder ID, source repository, build type, and `externalParameters` are each compared to expected values. 3) Answer no if any is missing, provenance is only generated in CI but not verified, or conditions use wildcards.\",\n          \"met\": \"no\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/deploy.yml:66\",\n          \"quote\": \"cosign verify\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"Only the signature is verified. Provenance is generated in CI (ci.yml:67) but nothing checks builder, source repo, build type or externalParameters (no verify-attestation).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.4\",\n          \"check\": \"The policy is in enforce mode, covers production namespaces, and denies images that match no policy.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Read the policy mode and scope (`validationFailureAction`, `failureAction`, `mode`, namespace selectors, exclusions). 2) Check for a no-match deny. 3) Answer no if mode is `Audit` or `warn`, production namespaces are excluded or unmatched, `failurePolicy: Ignore`, or images matching no policy are allowed.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No admission policy in the repo, so mode, namespace scope and no-match deny cannot be read.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B10.5\",\n          \"check\": \"The pinned Cosign or verifier version is at least 2.6.2 (2.x) or 3.0.4 (3.x).\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find Cosign or verifier versions in CI workflows (`cosign-installer`, `cosign-release`), Dockerfiles, and policy-controller charts. 2) Compare to 2.6.2 (2.x) and 3.0.4 (3.x). 3) Answer no if any pin is lower or uses `latest` or no version. Answer unknown if no verifier is in this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \".github/workflows/ci.yml:71\",\n          \"quote\": \"cosign-release: v2.6.2\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Both pins checked: ci.yml:71 and deploy.yml:60 are v2.6.2; no other cosign install.\",\n          \"note\": \"Cosign is pinned at 2.6.2 in CI and deploy.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"red_flags_found\": [],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"Check provenance fields such as the builder, source repository, build type, and the parameters set from outside the build\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"Deploy checks the image signature but never checks build provenance fields, and no admission policy is in the repo.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Add cosign verify-attestation for builder, source repo, build type and externalParameters, and an enforcing admission policy.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"infrastructure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"B11\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Minimal, isolated runtime\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Remove shells, downloaders, package managers, mounts, and privileges the agent doesn't need. As a container baseline, meet the Kubernetes Pod Security Standards \\\"restricted\\\" profile or the same controls elsewhere. That means non-root, no privilege escalation, all capabilities dropped, and a seccomp profile set. Where supported, also use a read-only root filesystem and user namespaces; the restricted profile doesn't require those two. For running untrusted code, use a sandbox that fits the threat, such as a microVM or a user-space kernel. Ordinary containers share the host's kernel. For managed runtimes, record the provider's isolation evidence and what you can't see. Test that host access is blocked. A blocked probe does not prove the sandbox resists every escape.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Container image not pinned by digest or signature-checked\",\n          \"owner\": \"B10\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Outbound traffic to unapproved internet destinations\",\n          \"owner\": \"B09\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Network path to admin systems or other tenants' resources\",\n          \"owner\": \"B08\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"likely_pass\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml\",\n          \"line\": 92,\n          \"note\": \"Pods and containers meet the restricted baseline; the reminder container inherits runAsNonRoot and seccomp from its pod.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B11.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Container settings set non-root, no privilege escalation, all capabilities dropped, and a seccomp profile, matching Pod Security 'restricted' or the same controls.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find pod `securityContext` and container `securityContext`, plus namespace labels. 2) Check `runAsNonRoot: true`, `allowPrivilegeEscalation: false`, `capabilities.drop: [ALL]`, `seccompProfile: RuntimeDefault`. 3) Answer no if any is missing on any container (including init and sidecars), set the wrong way, or overridden per container, or the Dockerfile runs as root with no override.\",\n          \"met\": \"yes\",\n          \"evidence\": \"k8s/deployment.yaml:92\",\n          \"quote\": \"drop: [\\\"ALL\\\"]\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"Read all four securityContexts: pod-level runAsNonRoot and seccomp RuntimeDefault (lines 67-74, 135-140) plus container allowPrivilegeEscalation false and drop ALL (86-94, 152-157). No init or sidecar containers. Namespace enforces restricted (line 6).\",\n          \"note\": \"Pods and containers meet the restricted baseline; the reminder container inherits runAsNonRoot and seccomp from its pod.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"B11.2\",\n          \"check\": \"The final image has no shell, downloader, or package manager the agent does not need.\",\n          \"verify\": \"