ite fails, AuditUnavailable is rethrown (line 92) after a side effect already happened, so the action is unrecorded.\"\n      ],\n      \"violates\": [\n        \"authorization decisions with the policy version used\"\n      ],\n      \"also_affects\": [\n        \"E11\",\n        \"R01\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"Executed actions are logged without arguments, results or policy version, and after the action runs.\",\n      \"next_step\": \"Fix policy.version, add key arguments and results, and write an attempt record before the call.\",\n      \"lead_role\": \"agent_team\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": \"R14\",\n      \"gate\": \"G2\",\n      \"title\": \"Recovery integrity\",\n      \"requirement\": \"If logs or checkpoints drive recovery, make them tamper-evident. Before using them, verify them against a separately protected trust anchor or signing key. Test that verification rejects changed checkpoints. It must also catch truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of a whole hash chain. For automatic recovery, confirm the destination supports idempotency: sending the same request twice has the effect of sending it once. Replay only within the destination's documented scope and time window. Confirm that actions you can't undo don't happen twice. Where support is missing or the result is unclear, check that replay pauses for reconciliation instead of sending again.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"What happens to in-flight writes and queued actions at stop\",\n          \"owner\": \"R12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Rollback to an approved earlier release not tested\",\n          \"owner\": \"C07\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Agent able to delete or rewrite its own audit history\",\n          \"owner\": \"E10\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"na_candidate\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"file\": \"s