fication uses a signed head or sequence number held outside the store. 2) Answer no if truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, or replacing the whole chain would still pass.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.4\",\n          \"check\": \"Automatic replay sends idempotency keys that the destination enforces, and only for integrations that support them.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find replay code. 2) Check it sends idempotency keys (`Idempotency-Key`, `client_token`) only to integrations that enforce them. 3) Answer no if replay sends without keys, uses a local dedupe table as the only guard, or replays to integrations without support.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"R14.5\",\n          \"check\": \"When idempotency is missing or the result is unclear, replay pauses for reconciliation instead of resending.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Find replay handling for unclear results or missing idempotency. 2) Answer no if replay resends instead of pausing for reconciliation, or retry is the default on timeout.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"No checkpoints or recovery logs drive recovery and nothing replays automatically (README.md:26); refunds carry a provider idempotency key (payments.ts:35).\"\n  